0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
BLACK SCREEN

1
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,620
I should've known that you would be here,

2
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:27,290
Professor McGonagall.

3
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:40,310
Good evening, Professor Dumbledore.

4
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:47,060
Are the rumors true, Albus?

5
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:49,190
I'm afraid so, professor.

6
00:01:49,730 --> 00:01:50,900
The good

7
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:52,400
and the bad.

8
00:01:52,690 --> 00:01:54,030
And the boy?

9
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,740
Hagrid is bringing him.

10
00:01:56,070 --> 00:01:57,280
Is it wise

11
00:01:57,370 --> 00:02:00,450
to trust Hagrid with something so important?

12
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:04,750
Professor, I would trust Hagrid with my life.

13
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:26,020
Professor Dumbledore, sir.

14
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:27,560
Professor McGonagall.

15
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,860
    No problems, I trust, Hagrid?

16
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:32,230
No, sir.

17
00:02:32,730 --> 00:02:36,400
Little tyke fell asleep as we were flying over Bristol.

18
00:02:38,030 --> 00:02:39,530
Try not to wake him.

19
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,580
There you go.

20
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:53,380
Do you really think it's safe, leaving him with these people?

21
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:55,050
I've watched them all day.

22
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:58,640
They're the worst sort of Muggles imaginable.

23
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:03,220
-They really are...  -The only family he has.

24
00:03:03,390 --> 00:03:05,100
He'll be famous.

25
00:03:05,230 --> 00:03:07,190
Every child in our world

26
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,400
will know his name.

27
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,690
Exactly.

28
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:13,820
He's far better off growing up away from all of that.

29
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:19,360
Until he's ready.

30
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,630
There, there, Hagrid.

31
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:36,380
It's not really goodbye, after all.

32
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:50,440
Good luck...

33
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:53,690
...Harry Potter.

34
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:14,000
Up. Get up!

35
00:04:17,130 --> 00:04:18,130
Now!

36
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:35,480
Wake up, cousin! We're going to the zoo!

37
00:04:45,870 --> 00:04:50,500
Here he comes, the birthday boy.

38
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:52,290
Happy birthday, son.

39
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:56,920
Cook breakfast. And try not to burn anything.

40
00:04:57,050 --> 00:04:58,510
Yes, Aunt Petunia.

41
00:04:58,590 --> 00:05:02,470
I want everything to be perfect...

42
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:05,720
...for my Dudley's special day!

43
00:05:05,850 --> 00:05:06,760
Hurry up!

44
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:08,470
Bring my coffee, boy.

45
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,560
Yes, Uncle Vernon.

46
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,850
Aren't they wonderful, darling?

47
00:05:17,110 --> 00:05:18,400
How many are there?

48
00:05:18,530 --> 00:05:20,440
36. Counted them myself.

49
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:23,910
36?! But last year I had 37!

50
00:05:24,030 --> 00:05:26,450
But some are bigger than last year's.

51
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:28,080
I don't care!

52
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:31,580
This is what we're going to do.

53
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:35,170
We're going to buy you two new presents. How's that, pumpkin?

54
00:05:39,170 --> 00:05:40,710
It should be a lovely day at the zoo.

55
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,420
I'm really looking forward to it.

56
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:48,390
I'm warning you now, boy.

57
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:52,100
Any funny business, any at all...

58
00:05:52,230 --> 00:05:55,810
...and you won't have any meals for a week.

59
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:56,900
Get in.

60
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:06,450
Make it move.

61
00:06:09,910 --> 00:06:11,040
Move!

62
00:06:11,790 --> 00:06:13,410
-Move!  -He's asleep!

63
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:16,040
He's boring.

64
00:06:19,590 --> 00:06:22,920
Sorry about him. He doesn't understand what it's like,

65
00:06:23,010 --> 00:06:25,340
lying there day after day...

66
00:06:25,470 --> 00:06:28,720
...watching people press their ugly faces in on you.

67
00:06:31,970 --> 00:06:33,770
Can you hear me?

68
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:38,610
It's just,

69
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:41,150
I've never talked to a snake before.

70
00:06:41,650 --> 00:06:43,230
Do you?

71
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:46,650
I means. Do you talk to people often?

72
00:06:48,410 --> 00:06:50,240
You're from Burma, aren't you?

73
00:06:50,530 --> 00:06:53,700
Was it nice there? Do you miss your family?

74
00:06:57,290 --> 00:06:58,670
I see.

75
00:06:58,830 --> 00:07:02,250
That's me as well. I never knew my parents either.

76
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,840
Moving. Mummy, Dad,

77
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:06,300
you won't believe what this snake is doing!

78
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,660
Thanks.

79
00:07:32,530 --> 00:07:33,700
Anytime.

80
00:07:37,410 --> 00:07:38,920
Snake!

81
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:58,230
Mum! Mummy! Help me!

82
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:01,940
My darling boy! How did you get in there?

83
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:05,070
Who did this? How did you get in there?

84
00:08:05,230 --> 00:08:07,740
Is there a snake?

85
00:08:11,910 --> 00:08:13,280
It's all right, sweetheart.

86
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:15,620
We'll get you out of these cold clothes.

87
00:08:18,710 --> 00:08:20,040
What happened?

88
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:21,880
I swear, I don't know!

89
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,670
The glass was there and then it was gone,

90
00:08:23,790 --> 00:08:25,250
like magic.

91
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:33,180
There's no such thing as magic.

92
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:12,680
Marge is ill. Ate a funny whelk.

93
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,180
Dad, look! Harry's got a letter!

94
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:15,800
Give back. It's mine!

95
00:09:16,010 --> 00:09:19,180
Yours? Who'd be writing to you?

96
00:09:52,670 --> 00:09:54,630
No more mail through this letterbox.

97
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:09,190
Have a lovely day at the office, dear.

98
00:10:12,690 --> 00:10:15,070
Go on.

99
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:42,350
Fine day, Sunday.

100
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:46,060
In my opinion, best day of the week.

101
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:47,600
Why is that, Dudley?

102
00:10:48,770 --> 00:10:50,400
Because there's no post on Sundays?

103
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:51,860
Right you are, Harry!

104
00:10:53,230 --> 00:10:54,900
No post on Sunday.

105
00:10:57,410 --> 00:11:01,740
No blasted letters today! No, sir.

106
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:06,410
Not one single bloody letter. Not one!

107
00:11:15,050 --> 00:11:19,140
No, sir, not one blasted, miserable...

108
00:11:29,270 --> 00:11:30,310
Oh, no!

109
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:33,230
Make it stop, please!

110
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:37,610
Make it stop, please!

111
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:40,910
Stop! Stop it!

112
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:43,330
Mummy, what's happening?

113
00:11:43,450 --> 00:11:44,740
What's this?

114
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:48,620
Give me that!

115
00:11:49,420 --> 00:11:51,380
Give me that letter!

116
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,510
Get off!

117
00:11:59,630 --> 00:12:03,050
They're my letters! Let go of me!

118
00:12:04,510 --> 00:12:07,980
That's it! We're going away!

119
00:12:08,270 --> 00:12:12,110
Far away, where they can't find us!

120
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:14,360
Daddy's gone mad, hasn't he?

121
00:12:50,190 --> 00:12:51,810
Make a wish, Harry.

122
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:09,700
Who's there?

123
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,390
Sorry about that.

124
00:13:32,230 --> 00:13:34,270
I demand that you leave at once.

125
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,060
You are breaking and entering.

126
00:13:39,530 --> 00:13:42,530
Dry up, Dursley, you great prune.

127
00:13:47,780 --> 00:13:49,240
I haven't seen you

128
00:13:49,330 --> 00:13:50,870
since you was a baby, Harry.But...

129
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:53,000
You're a bit more along than I expected.

130
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,500
Particularly in the middle.

131
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:58,090
I'm not Harry.

132
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,470
I am.

133
00:14:03,090 --> 00:14:05,090
Well, of course you are.

134
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:06,970
Got something for you.

135
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:09,680
Afraid I sat on it,

136
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:12,180
but I imagine it'll taste fine just the same.

137
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,940
Baked it myself, words and all.

138
00:14:24,450 --> 00:14:25,320
Thank you.

139
00:14:25,450 --> 00:14:29,120
It's not every day your young man turns 11, is it?

140
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,760
Excuse me, but...

141
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:49,010
who are you?

142
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:50,850
Rubeus Hagrid,

143
00:14:50,850 --> 00:14:54,180
keeper of keys and Grounds at Hogwarts.

144
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:56,560
Of course, you know about Hogwarts.

145
00:14:56,730 --> 00:14:58,480
Sorry, no.

146
00:14:58,610 --> 00:15:00,570
No? Blot me, Harry

147
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:03,150
Didn't you ever wonder where your mum and dad learned it all?

148
00:15:03,530 --> 00:15:05,110
Learned what?

149
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:07,070
You're a wizard, Harry.

150
00:15:08,910 --> 00:15:10,240
I'm a what?

151
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:11,540
A wizard.

152
00:15:11,540 --> 00:15:14,540
A good one, I'd wager, once you're trained up.

153
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:16,330
No, you've made a mistake.

154
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:17,580
I mean...

155
00:15:17,670 --> 00:15:21,000
...I can't be a wizard.

156
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,630
I mean, I'm just...

157
00:15:23,710 --> 00:15:26,470
Harry. Just Harry.

158
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:29,470
Well, Just Harry,

159
00:15:29,590 --> 00:15:31,350
did you ever make anything happen?

160
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:34,850
Anything you couldn't explain, when you were angry or scared?

161
00:15:52,530 --> 00:15:53,910
Dear Mr. Potter,

162
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,620
We are pleased to inform you...

163
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:59,210
...that you have accepted at Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry."

164
00:15:59,330 --> 00:16:01,670
He will not be going! I told you.

165
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:04,380
We swore we'd put a stop to all this rubbish.

166
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:05,960
You knew?

167
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:08,800
You knew all along and you never told me?

168
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:10,390
Of course we knew.

169
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:12,300
How could you not be?

170
00:16:12,390 --> 00:16:16,060
My perfect sister being who she was.

171
00:16:16,270 --> 00:16:21,860
My mother and father were so proud the day she got her letter.

172
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:26,190
We have a witch in the family. Isn't it wonderful?

173
00:16:26,650 --> 00:16:29,900
I was the only one to see her for what she was.

174
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,370
A freak!

175
00:16:32,570 --> 00:16:35,490
Then she met that Potter, and then she had you...

176
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:36,910
...and I knew you would be the same.

177
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:41,460
Just as strange, just as abnormal.

178
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:44,750
And then she got herself blown up,

179
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,590
and we got landed with you

180
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:50,930
Blown up? You told me my parents died in a car crash.

181
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:52,760
A car crash?

182
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:55,760
A car crash killed Lily and James Potter?

183
00:16:55,850 --> 00:16:56,600
We had to say something.

184
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:59,730
It's an outrage! A scandal!

185
00:16:59,850 --> 00:17:01,390
He'll not be going.

186
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:05,940
A great Muggle like you is going to stop him?

187
00:17:06,070 --> 00:17:07,150
Muggle?

188
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:08,490
Non-magic folk.

189
00:17:08,610 --> 00:17:11,150
This boy's had his name down since he were born.

190
00:17:11,450 --> 00:17:14,870
He's going to the finest school of witchcraft and wizardry.

191
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:19,500
He'll be under the finest headmaster Hogwarts has seen,

192
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:21,410
Albus Dumbledore.

193
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:26,040
I will not pay to have a crackpot old fool teach him magic tricks.

194
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:27,960
Never ...

195
00:17:28,090 --> 00:17:32,800
insult Albus Dumbledore in front of me.

196
00:17:51,530 --> 00:17:56,200
I'd appreciate it if you didn't tell anyone at Hogwarts about that.

197
00:17:56,530 --> 00:17:59,040
I'm not allowed to do magic.

198
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:00,160
Okay.

199
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:05,190
We're a bit behind schedule. Best be off.

200
00:18:11,550 --> 00:18:14,130
Unless you'd rather stay, of course.

201
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:32,320
All students must be equipped with...

202
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:35,490
...one standard size 2 pewter cauldron...

203
00:18:35,570 --> 00:18:37,570
...and may bring, if they desire,

204
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:40,870
either an owl, a cat or a toad.

205
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:44,040
Can we find all this in London?

206
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:46,000
If you know where to go.

207
00:19:09,610 --> 00:19:12,690
Ah, Hagrid! The usual, I presume?

208
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:13,570
No, thanks, Tom.

209
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:15,950
I'm on official Hogwarts business.

210
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:20,030
Just helping young Harry buy his school supplies.

211
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,620
Bless my soul.

212
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:23,660
It's Harry Potter!

213
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,710
Welcome back, Mr. Potter.

214
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:31,290
Welcome back.

215
00:19:31,710 --> 00:19:33,210
Doris Crockford. Mr. Potter.

216
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:36,420
I can't believe I'm meeting you at last.

217
00:19:36,510 --> 00:19:39,510
Harry Potter.

218
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,680
Can't tell you how pleased I am to meet you.

219
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:44,520
Hello, professor. I didn't see you.

220
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,520
Harry, this's Professor Quirrell

221
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:49,900
will be your Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher.

222
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:51,770
Oh, nice to meet you.

223
00:19:52,570 --> 00:19:55,530
Fearfully fascinating subject.

224
00:19:55,610 --> 00:20:00,120
Not that you need it, eh, Potter?

225
00:20:01,490 --> 00:20:05,950
Yes, well, must be going now. Lots to buy.

226
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,160
Goodbye.

227
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:11,920
See, Harry? You're famous.

228
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,960
But why am I famous, Hagrid?

229
00:20:14,050 --> 00:20:17,630
All those people, how is it they know who I am?

230
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:21,050
I'm not sure I'm the right person to tell you that, Harry.

231
00:20:38,530 --> 00:20:41,530
Welcome, Harry, to Diagon Alley.

232
00:20:58,630 --> 00:21:00,930
Here, you get your quills and ink.

233
00:21:01,380 --> 00:21:04,510
Over there, all your bits and bobs for doing wizardry.

234
00:21:30,750 --> 00:21:32,120
It's a world-class racing broom.

235
00:21:32,210 --> 00:21:36,340
Look at it! The new Nimbus 2000!

236
00:21:36,750 --> 00:21:39,260
It's the fastest model yet.

237
00:21:44,090 --> 00:21:47,010
But how am I to pay for all this?

238
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:48,560
I haven't any money.

239
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,140
There's your money, Harry.

240
00:21:50,230 --> 00:21:52,020
Gringotts, the wizard bank.

241
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:54,520
Ain't no safer place, not one.

242
00:21:54,600 --> 00:21:56,310
Except perhaps Hogwarts.

243
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:11,660
Hagrid,

244
00:22:12,330 --> 00:22:14,370
what exactly are these things?

245
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:16,420
They're goblins, Harry.

246
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:20,000
Clever as they come, but not the most friendly of beasts.

247
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:21,710
Best stay close.

248
00:22:25,930 --> 00:22:29,140
Mr. Harry Potter wishes to make a withdrawal.

249
00:22:33,850 --> 00:22:37,860
And does Mr. Harry Potter have his key?

250
00:22:37,980 --> 00:22:40,530
Wait a minute. Got it here somewhere.

251
00:22:44,860 --> 00:22:46,320
Ha! There's the little devil.

252
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:49,410
And there's something else as well.

253
00:22:51,290 --> 00:22:53,410
Professor Dumbledore gave me this.

254
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:03,210
It's about You-know-What in vault you-know-which.

255
00:23:04,970 --> 00:23:06,090
Very well.

256
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:14,430
Vault 687.

257
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:18,190
Lamp, please.

258
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:28,820
Key, please.

259
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:55,600
Did you think your parents would leave you with nothing?

260
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:59,900
Vault 713.

261
00:24:00,020 --> 00:24:01,360
What's in there, Hagrid?

262
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:02,860
Can't tell you, Harry.

263
00:24:03,020 --> 00:24:05,820
Hogwarts business. Very secret.

264
00:24:05,900 --> 00:24:07,150
Stand back.

265
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:38,270
Best not to mention this to anyone.

266
00:24:46,900 --> 00:24:49,030
I still need...

267
00:24:49,150 --> 00:24:50,360
a wand.

268
00:24:50,910 --> 00:24:53,530
A wand? You want OIlivanders.

269
00:24:53,660 --> 00:24:54,830
There ain't no place better.

270
00:24:55,450 --> 00:24:57,370
Run along there and wait.

271
00:24:57,450 --> 00:24:59,960
I got one more thing to do. Won't be long.

272
00:25:18,390 --> 00:25:19,640
Hello?

273
00:25:23,020 --> 00:25:24,060
Hello?

274
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:31,200
I wondered when I'd be seeing you,

275
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:32,610
Mr. Potter.

276
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:42,870
It seems only yesterday...

277
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:48,090
...that your mother and father were in here buying their first wands.

278
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:57,470
Here we are.

279
00:26:06,360 --> 00:26:08,190
Give it a wave.

280
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:17,120
Apparently not.

281
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:27,130
Perhaps...

282
00:26:29,250 --> 00:26:30,670
...this.

283
00:26:38,470 --> 00:26:41,350
No, no, definitely not.

284
00:26:42,180 --> 00:26:43,480
No matter.

285
00:26:50,360 --> 00:26:52,650
I wonder...

286
00:27:21,260 --> 00:27:23,220
Curious.

287
00:27:23,770 --> 00:27:25,890
Very curious.

288
00:27:26,980 --> 00:27:30,690
Sorry, but what's curious?

289
00:27:31,610 --> 00:27:33,400
I remember every wand I've ever sold,

290
00:27:33,530 --> 00:27:34,610
Mr. Potter.

291
00:27:35,150 --> 00:27:36,450
It so happens that...

292
00:27:36,570 --> 00:27:40,740
the phoenix whose tail feather resides in your wand,

293
00:27:40,830 --> 00:27:43,330
gave another feather...

294
00:27:43,450 --> 00:27:46,460
just one other.

295
00:27:46,580 --> 00:27:47,790
It is curious

296
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:51,040
that you should be destined for this wand...

297
00:27:51,170 --> 00:27:54,300
...when its brother gave you

298
00:27:54,420 --> 00:27:56,050
that scar.

299
00:27:58,430 --> 00:28:01,140
And who owned that wand?

300
00:28:01,260 --> 00:28:05,520
We do not speak his name.

301
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:09,150
The wand chooses the wizard, Mr. Potter.

302
00:28:09,270 --> 00:28:12,230
It's not always clear why.

303
00:28:12,570 --> 00:28:16,400
But I think it is clear...

304
00:28:16,490 --> 00:28:19,740
...that we can expect great things from you.

305
00:28:20,410 --> 00:28:22,200
After all,

306
00:28:22,280 --> 00:28:24,950
He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named...

307
00:28:25,040 --> 00:28:27,620
...did great things.

308
00:28:27,750 --> 00:28:31,580
Terrible...yes,

309
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:34,800
but great.

310
00:28:39,180 --> 00:28:41,090
Harry! Harry!

311
00:28:41,640 --> 00:28:43,220
Happy birthday.

312
00:28:51,150 --> 00:28:54,320
You all right, Harry? You seem very quiet.

313
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:58,150
He killed my parents, didn't he?

314
00:28:58,280 --> 00:29:00,070
The one who gave me this.

315
00:29:00,860 --> 00:29:02,660
You know, Hagrid.

316
00:29:03,280 --> 00:29:04,780
I know you do.

317
00:29:08,330 --> 00:29:10,170
First, and understand this, Harry,

318
00:29:10,290 --> 00:29:12,130
because it's very important:

319
00:29:13,080 --> 00:29:15,300
Not all wizards are good.

320
00:29:15,670 --> 00:29:17,010
Some of them go bad.

321
00:29:17,130 --> 00:29:18,170
A few years ago...

322
00:29:18,300 --> 00:29:20,720
...there was a wizard who went as bad as you can go.

323
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:23,800
His name was V...

324
00:29:24,050 --> 00:29:25,810
His name was V...

325
00:29:25,890 --> 00:29:27,390
Maybe if you wrote it down?

326
00:29:27,520 --> 00:29:30,940
No, I can't spell it. All right,

327
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:32,810
Voldemort.

328
00:29:32,900 --> 00:29:34,400
Voldemort?

329
00:29:38,030 --> 00:29:40,240
It was dark times, Harry.

330
00:29:42,490 --> 00:29:45,740
Voldemort started to gather some followers.

331
00:29:45,870 --> 00:29:48,500
Brought them over to the Dark Side.

332
00:29:50,540 --> 00:29:53,670
Anyone that stood up to him ended up dead.

333
00:29:54,790 --> 00:29:57,460
Your parents fought against him.

334
00:29:58,250 --> 00:30:01,010
But nobody lived once he decided to kill them.

335
00:30:06,140 --> 00:30:08,350
Nobody, not one.

336
00:30:09,020 --> 00:30:10,480
Except you.

337
00:30:13,020 --> 00:30:17,900
Me? Voldemort tried to kill me?

338
00:30:17,980 --> 00:30:22,450
Yes. That ain't no ordinary cut on your forehead, Harry.

339
00:30:22,570 --> 00:30:25,700
A mark like that only comes from being touched by a curse,

340
00:30:25,780 --> 00:30:27,870
an evil curse.

341
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:32,830
What happened to V...? To You-know-Who?

342
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:36,250
Well, some say he died.

343
00:30:36,750 --> 00:30:39,210
Codswallop, in my opinion.

344
00:30:39,300 --> 00:30:43,130
Nope, I reckon he's out there still...

345
00:30:43,260 --> 00:30:45,720
...too tired to carry on.

346
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:48,050
But one thing's certain.

347
00:30:48,140 --> 00:30:51,560
Something about you stumped him that night.

348
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:53,180
That's why you're famous.

349
00:30:53,310 --> 00:30:56,350
That's why everybody knows your name.

350
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:59,690
You're the boy who lived.

351
00:31:09,450 --> 00:31:10,950
What are you looking at?

352
00:31:14,040 --> 00:31:15,830
Blimey, is that the time?

353
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:17,540
Sorry Harry. I'm gonna have to leave you.

354
00:31:17,630 --> 00:31:20,250
Dumbledore will be wanting his...

355
00:31:20,340 --> 00:31:22,090
Well, he'll be wanting to see me.

356
00:31:22,170 --> 00:31:25,010
Your train leaves in 10 minutes.

357
00:31:25,130 --> 00:31:26,340
Here's your ticket.

358
00:31:26,470 --> 00:31:29,470
Stick to your ticket, that's very important.

359
00:31:33,560 --> 00:31:35,980
Platform 93/4?

360
00:31:36,060 --> 00:31:38,690
But, Hagrid, there must be a mistake.

361
00:31:38,810 --> 00:31:40,900
This says platform 93/4.

362
00:31:41,020 --> 00:31:43,230
There's no such thing, is there?

363
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:58,630
Keep off the doors.

364
00:32:02,840 --> 00:32:03,840
Sorry.

365
00:32:06,130 --> 00:32:08,510
Excuse me. Excuse me.

366
00:32:09,140 --> 00:32:10,640
On your left, Madam.

367
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:11,760
Excuse me, Sir.

368
00:32:11,850 --> 00:32:14,520
Can you tell me where I might find platform 93/4?

369
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:15,930
Platform 93/4?

370
00:32:16,020 --> 00:32:17,140
Think you're being funny, do you?

371
00:32:17,270 --> 00:32:20,980
It's the same every year, packed with Muggles. Come on.

372
00:32:21,270 --> 00:32:23,360
-Muggles?   -Platform 93/4, this way.

373
00:32:30,370 --> 00:32:32,530
All right, Percy, you first.

374
00:32:43,460 --> 00:32:44,960
Fred, you next.

375
00:32:45,130 --> 00:32:46,420
He's not Fred, I am.

376
00:32:46,550 --> 00:32:48,880
You call yourself our mother?

377
00:32:48,970 --> 00:32:51,090
I'm sorry, George.

378
00:32:54,890 --> 00:32:56,890
I'm only joking. I am Fred.

379
00:33:03,150 --> 00:33:04,570
Excuse me.

380
00:33:06,820 --> 00:33:08,650
Could you tell me

381
00:33:08,740 --> 00:33:09,820
how to?

382
00:33:09,900 --> 00:33:11,820
How to get onto the platform?

383
00:33:11,910 --> 00:33:13,410
Not to worry, dear.

384
00:33:13,530 --> 00:33:16,040
It's Ron's first time to Hogwarts as well.

385
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:18,080
All you do is

386
00:33:18,200 --> 00:33:22,250
walk straight at the wall between platforms 9 and 10.

387
00:33:22,380 --> 00:33:24,380
Best to run if you're nervous.

388
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:25,590
Good luck.

389
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:24,940
Excuse me.

390
00:34:25,060 --> 00:34:27,900
Do you mind? Everywhere else is full.

391
00:34:28,020 --> 00:34:29,280
Not at all.

392
00:34:33,150 --> 00:34:34,490
I'm Ron, by the way.

393
00:34:34,610 --> 00:34:35,700
Ron Weasley.

394
00:34:35,820 --> 00:34:37,490
I'm Harry. Harry Potter.

395
00:34:39,830 --> 00:34:41,960
So...so it's true!

396
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:45,500
I mean, do you really have the?

397
00:34:45,630 --> 00:34:47,090
The what?

398
00:34:47,670 --> 00:34:48,750
The scar?

399
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:50,960
Oh. yeah.

400
00:34:51,550 --> 00:34:52,880
Wicked!

401
00:34:56,260 --> 00:34:57,850
Anything off the trolley, dears?

402
00:34:57,970 --> 00:35:01,060
No, thanks. I'm all set.

403
00:35:05,350 --> 00:35:06,940
We'll take the lot.

404
00:35:18,530 --> 00:35:20,370
Bertie Bott's Every Flavor Beans?

405
00:35:20,490 --> 00:35:22,700
They mean every flavor.

406
00:35:23,540 --> 00:35:27,130
There's chocolate and peppermint and also...

407
00:35:27,210 --> 00:35:30,460
...spinach, liver and tripe.

408
00:35:31,300 --> 00:35:34,670
George sweared he got a booger-flavored one once.

409
00:35:40,140 --> 00:35:41,810
Are they real frogs?

410
00:35:41,890 --> 00:35:43,140
It's a spell.

411
00:35:43,220 --> 00:35:45,560
Beside the cards you want.

412
00:35:45,640 --> 00:35:47,980
Each pack's got a famous witch or wizard.

413
00:35:48,100 --> 00:35:50,020
I've got about 500 meself.

414
00:35:52,690 --> 00:35:54,070
Watch it!

415
00:35:56,990 --> 00:35:58,700
That's rotten luck.

416
00:35:58,820 --> 00:36:01,240
They've only got one good jump in them.

417
00:36:03,540 --> 00:36:05,040
I've got Dumbledore!

418
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:06,960
I got about six of him.

419
00:36:09,290 --> 00:36:10,460
Hey, he's gone!

420
00:36:10,590 --> 00:36:14,210
You can't expect him to hang around all day, can you?

421
00:36:15,090 --> 00:36:16,760
This is Scabbers. By the way.

422
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:18,300
Pathetic, isn't he?

423
00:36:18,430 --> 00:36:19,640
A  little.

424
00:36:19,760 --> 00:36:22,350
Fred gave me a spell to turn him yellow.

425
00:36:22,350 --> 00:36:23,350
Want to see?

426
00:36:23,430 --> 00:36:24,430
Yeah.

427
00:36:29,440 --> 00:36:31,060
Sun...

428
00:36:32,270 --> 00:36:34,190
Has anyone seen a toad?

429
00:36:34,280 --> 00:36:36,030
A boy named Neville's lost one.

430
00:36:36,110 --> 00:36:37,400
No.

431
00:36:37,490 --> 00:36:39,360
Oh, are you doing magic?

432
00:36:39,450 --> 00:36:40,870
Let's see, then.

433
00:36:42,870 --> 00:36:47,290
Sunshine, daisies, butter mellow

434
00:36:47,410 --> 00:36:50,080
Turn this stupid, fat rat yellow

435
00:36:53,250 --> 00:36:55,960
Are you sure that's a real spell?

436
00:36:56,090 --> 00:36:58,630
Well, it's not very good, is it?

437
00:36:59,050 --> 00:36:59,800
Of course.

438
00:36:59,880 --> 00:37:02,300
I've only tried a few simple ones myself...

439
00:37:02,430 --> 00:37:04,010
...but they've all worked for me.

440
00:37:08,730 --> 00:37:10,100
For example,

441
00:37:10,980 --> 00:37:13,270
Oculus Reparo.

442
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:17,990
That's better, isn't it?

443
00:37:20,110 --> 00:37:23,870
Holy cricket, you're Harry Potter!

444
00:37:23,990 --> 00:37:25,450
I'm Hermione Granger.

445
00:37:25,540 --> 00:37:27,950
And you are?

446
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:30,170
I'm Ron Weasley.

447
00:37:30,290 --> 00:37:31,370
Pleasure.

448
00:37:31,670 --> 00:37:33,750
You two better change into robes.

449
00:37:33,840 --> 00:37:35,710
I expect we'll be arriving soon.

450
00:37:40,840 --> 00:37:44,600
You've got dirt on your nose. Did you know?

451
00:37:44,680 --> 00:37:45,970
Just there.

452
00:37:58,860 --> 00:38:00,950
Right, then. First years,

453
00:38:01,030 --> 00:38:02,570
this way, please!

454
00:38:02,950 --> 00:38:05,370
Come on, first years, don't be shy.

455
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:08,120
Come on now, hurry up.

456
00:38:15,130 --> 00:38:16,250
Hello, Harry.

457
00:38:16,380 --> 00:38:17,500
Hi, Hagrid.

458
00:38:19,210 --> 00:38:20,880
Right, then. This way to the boats.

459
00:38:21,010 --> 00:38:22,430
Come on now, follow me.

460
00:39:09,190 --> 00:39:10,990
Wicked.

461
00:39:39,290 --> 00:39:41,420
Welcome to Hogwarts.

462
00:39:41,590 --> 00:39:44,510
Shortly, you'll pass through these doors

463
00:39:44,630 --> 00:39:45,840
and join your classmates.

464
00:39:45,970 --> 00:39:47,640
But before you take your seats,

465
00:39:47,760 --> 00:39:50,760
you must be sorted into your houses.

466
00:39:51,140 --> 00:39:54,310
They are Gryffindor, Hufflepuff...

467
00:39:54,430 --> 00:39:58,520
...Ravenclaw and Slytherin.

468
00:39:59,400 --> 00:40:01,650
While you're here,

469
00:40:01,780 --> 00:40:04,610
your house will be like your family.

470
00:40:04,990 --> 00:40:08,320
Your triumphs will earn you points.

471
00:40:08,450 --> 00:40:12,580
Any rule-breaking and you will lose points.

472
00:40:13,080 --> 00:40:17,170
At the end of the year, the house with the most points

473
00:40:17,290 --> 00:40:18,710
wins the house cup.

474
00:40:18,830 --> 00:40:19,960
Trevor!

475
00:40:29,010 --> 00:40:30,260
Sorry.

476
00:40:30,680 --> 00:40:34,020
The Sorting Ceremony will begin momentarily.

477
00:40:35,730 --> 00:40:37,270
It's true then,

478
00:40:37,640 --> 00:40:39,600
what they're saying on the train.

479
00:40:39,730 --> 00:40:42,480
Harry Potter has come to Hogwarts.

480
00:40:42,690 --> 00:40:44,320
Harry Potter?

481
00:40:44,730 --> 00:40:49,030
This is Crabbe and Goyle. And I'm Malfoy.

482
00:40:50,070 --> 00:40:52,120
Draco Malfoy.

483
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:56,040
Think my name's funny, do you?

484
00:40:56,160 --> 00:40:58,000
I've no need to ask yours.

485
00:40:58,080 --> 00:41:01,290
Red hair and a hand-me-down robe?

486
00:41:01,380 --> 00:41:03,710
You must be a Weasley.

487
00:41:04,920 --> 00:41:07,130
You'll find out some wizarding families

488
00:41:07,220 --> 00:41:09,050
are better than others.

489
00:41:09,130 --> 00:41:12,550
You don't want to go making friends with the wrong sort.

490
00:41:13,050 --> 00:41:15,010
I can help you there.

491
00:41:17,430 --> 00:41:20,600
I think I can tell the wrong sort for myself, thanks.

492
00:41:27,070 --> 00:41:28,860
We're ready for you now. Follow me.

493
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:49,800
The ceiling isn't real. It's bewitched

494
00:41:49,920 --> 00:41:52,090
to look like the night sky.

495
00:41:52,550 --> 00:41:56,010
I read about it in Hogwarts, A History.

496
00:42:08,900 --> 00:42:10,450
Will you wait along here, please?

497
00:42:13,070 --> 00:42:15,830
Now, before we begin...

498
00:42:15,950 --> 00:42:19,250
...Professor Dumbledore would like to say a few words.

499
00:42:19,580 --> 00:42:24,130
I have a few start-of-term notices I wish to announce.

500
00:42:24,630 --> 00:42:26,920
The first years, please note...

501
00:42:27,130 --> 00:42:32,340
...that the Dark Forest is strictly forbidden to all students.

502
00:42:33,380 --> 00:42:36,930
Also, our caretaker, Mr. Filch,

503
00:42:37,010 --> 00:42:39,100
has asked me to remind you...

504
00:42:39,180 --> 00:42:43,900
...that the third-floor corridor is out of bounds...

505
00:42:43,980 --> 00:42:48,440
...to everyone who does not wish to die a most painful death.

506
00:42:49,610 --> 00:42:50,990
Thank you.

507
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:55,700
When I call your name,

508
00:42:55,820 --> 00:42:57,620
you will come forth.

509
00:42:57,700 --> 00:43:00,660
I shall place the Sorting Hat on your head...

510
00:43:01,500 --> 00:43:03,620
...and you will be sorted into your houses.

511
00:43:04,830 --> 00:43:06,790
Hermione Granger.

512
00:43:09,750 --> 00:43:11,010
Oh, no.

513
00:43:11,130 --> 00:43:12,470
Okay, relax.

514
00:43:12,840 --> 00:43:15,300
Mental, that one, I'm telling you.

515
00:43:20,560 --> 00:43:23,180
Right,

516
00:43:23,310 --> 00:43:25,650
then. Right.

517
00:43:25,730 --> 00:43:27,190
Okay.

518
00:43:27,270 --> 00:43:28,900
Gryffindor!

519
00:43:37,950 --> 00:43:39,910
Draco Malfoy.

520
00:43:45,460 --> 00:43:46,920
Slytherin!

521
00:43:48,590 --> 00:43:50,630
Every wizard who went bad

522
00:43:50,750 --> 00:43:51,710
was in Slytherin.

523
00:43:51,800 --> 00:43:53,130
Susan Bones.

524
00:44:02,600 --> 00:44:04,980
Harry, what is it?

525
00:44:05,100 --> 00:44:08,230
Nothing. Nothing, I'm fine.

526
00:44:08,350 --> 00:44:09,810
Let's see...

527
00:44:09,900 --> 00:44:11,270
I know!

528
00:44:11,480 --> 00:44:12,900
Hufflepuff!

529
00:44:15,530 --> 00:44:17,660
Ronald Weasley.

530
00:44:31,210 --> 00:44:34,170
Another Weasley!

531
00:44:34,260 --> 00:44:37,800
I know just what to do with you.

532
00:44:37,930 --> 00:44:39,930
Gryffindor!

533
00:44:46,350 --> 00:44:47,890
Harry Potter.

534
00:45:05,950 --> 00:45:09,870
Difficult, very difficult.

535
00:45:10,000 --> 00:45:14,090
Plenty of courage, I see. Not a bad mind, either.

536
00:45:14,210 --> 00:45:16,840
There's talent, oh, yes.

537
00:45:16,920 --> 00:45:20,760
And a thirst to prove yourself.

538
00:45:20,840 --> 00:45:23,600
But where to put you?

539
00:45:23,680 --> 00:45:26,220
Not Slytherin, not Slytherin!

540
00:45:26,350 --> 00:45:28,810
Not Slytherin, eh?

541
00:45:28,890 --> 00:45:32,110
Are you sure? You could be great, you know.

542
00:45:32,190 --> 00:45:35,320
It's all here, in your head.

543
00:45:35,440 --> 00:45:39,030
And Slytherin will help you on the way to greatness,

544
00:45:39,150 --> 00:45:40,820
no doubt about that.

545
00:45:40,950 --> 00:45:45,740
No? Well, if you're sure.

546
00:45:45,830 --> 00:45:47,660
Better be...

547
00:45:47,790 --> 00:45:49,790
...Gryffindor!

548
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:55,630
Welcome Potter.

549
00:45:57,920 --> 00:46:01,470
Welcome Potter.

550
00:46:15,360 --> 00:46:17,190
Your attention, please.

551
00:46:20,110 --> 00:46:23,320
Let the feast begin.

552
00:46:39,880 --> 00:46:41,300
I'm half and half.

553
00:46:41,470 --> 00:46:44,510
Me dad's a Muggle. Mum's a witch.

554
00:46:44,890 --> 00:46:47,560
Bit of a nasty shock for him when he found out.

555
00:46:49,560 --> 00:46:51,060
Percy,

556
00:46:51,180 --> 00:46:53,560
who's that teacher talking to Professor Quirrell?

557
00:46:53,650 --> 00:46:55,060
Professor Snape,

558
00:46:55,150 --> 00:46:56,690
head of Slytherin house.

559
00:46:56,900 --> 00:46:57,900
What's he teach?

560
00:46:57,980 --> 00:46:58,980
Potions.

561
00:46:59,110 --> 00:47:01,190
But he fancies the Dark Arts.

562
00:47:01,320 --> 00:47:03,740
He's been after Quirrell's job for years.

563
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:14,370
Hello! How are you? Welcome to Gryffindor.

564
00:47:25,180 --> 00:47:26,930
It's the Bloody Baron!

565
00:47:32,430 --> 00:47:33,350
Hello, Sir Nicholas.

566
00:47:33,440 --> 00:47:34,850
Have a nice summer?

567
00:47:35,310 --> 00:47:36,310
Dismal.

568
00:47:36,310 --> 00:47:40,020
Once again, my request to join the Headless Hunt has been denied.

569
00:47:43,780 --> 00:47:45,160
I know you.

570
00:47:45,280 --> 00:47:46,870
You're Nearly Headless Nick.

571
00:47:46,950 --> 00:47:49,780
I prefer Sir Nicholas, if you don't mind.

572
00:47:49,910 --> 00:47:51,410
Nearly headless?

573
00:47:51,490 --> 00:47:53,620
How can you be nearly headless?

574
00:47:53,750 --> 00:47:55,080
Like this.

575
00:48:05,720 --> 00:48:07,390
Gryffindors, follow me, please.

576
00:48:07,470 --> 00:48:08,930
I keep up. Thank you.

577
00:48:09,850 --> 00:48:11,390
Ravenclaw, follow me.

578
00:48:12,310 --> 00:48:13,520
This way.

579
00:48:14,270 --> 00:48:17,150
This is the most direct path to the dormitories.

580
00:48:17,270 --> 00:48:21,270
I keep an eye on the staircases. They like to change.

581
00:48:31,200 --> 00:48:33,370
Keep up, please, and follow me.

582
00:48:33,910 --> 00:48:36,830
Quickly now, come on. Come on.

583
00:48:37,290 --> 00:48:39,330
That picture's moving.

584
00:48:40,090 --> 00:48:42,840
-Look at that one.   -I think she fancies you.

585
00:48:45,260 --> 00:48:46,670
Look! Look!

586
00:48:46,800 --> 00:48:47,840
Who's that girl?

587
00:48:48,010 --> 00:48:50,350
Welcome to Hogwarts.

588
00:48:52,430 --> 00:48:53,310
Who's that?

589
00:49:06,190 --> 00:49:07,990
Password?

590
00:49:07,990 --> 00:49:10,160
Caput Draconis.

591
00:49:17,670 --> 00:49:19,090
Follow me, everyone. Keep up.

592
00:49:19,340 --> 00:49:21,590
Quickly, come on.

593
00:49:25,260 --> 00:49:26,720
Gather around here.

594
00:49:29,350 --> 00:49:32,020
Welcome to the Gryffindor common room.

595
00:49:32,850 --> 00:49:35,350
Boys' dormitory is upstairs to the left.

596
00:49:35,440 --> 00:49:37,360
Girls, the same on your right.

597
00:49:37,480 --> 00:49:40,610
Your belongings have already been brought up.

598
00:50:47,970 --> 00:50:50,300
Made it!

599
00:50:50,640 --> 00:50:53,930
Can you imagine the look on old McGonagall's face if we were late?

600
00:50:58,440 --> 00:51:00,400
That was bloody brilliant!

601
00:51:00,480 --> 00:51:03,190
Thank you for that assessment.

602
00:51:03,360 --> 00:51:05,280
It'd be better if I transfigured

603
00:51:05,400 --> 00:51:07,990
Mr. Potter and you into a watch.

604
00:51:08,110 --> 00:51:09,950
Then one of you might be on time.

605
00:51:10,070 --> 00:51:11,370
We got lost.

606
00:51:11,450 --> 00:51:13,370
Then perhaps a map?

607
00:51:13,830 --> 00:51:16,330
I trust you don't need one to find your seats.

608
00:51:25,420 --> 00:51:27,510
There will be no foolish wand-waving

609
00:51:27,630 --> 00:51:30,720
or silly incantations in this class.

610
00:51:31,260 --> 00:51:32,720
As such,

611
00:51:32,850 --> 00:51:35,220
I don't expect many of you to appreciate...

612
00:51:35,310 --> 00:51:38,440
...the subtle science and exact art that is potion-making.

613
00:51:38,560 --> 00:51:42,900
However, for those select few...

614
00:51:42,980 --> 00:51:47,440
...who possess the predisposition...

615
00:51:49,950 --> 00:51:53,780
...I can teach you how to bewitch the mind...

616
00:51:53,870 --> 00:51:56,580
...and ensnare the senses.

617
00:51:56,660 --> 00:52:00,750
I can tell you how to bottle fame brew glory

618
00:52:00,870 --> 00:52:04,960
and even put a stopper in death.

619
00:52:09,630 --> 00:52:11,590
Then again,

620
00:52:11,680 --> 00:52:14,180
maybe some of you have come to Hogwarts

621
00:52:14,260 --> 00:52:16,810
in possession of abilities...

622
00:52:16,930 --> 00:52:19,480
...so formidable that you feel confident enough...

623
00:52:19,600 --> 00:52:22,850
...to not pay attention.

624
00:52:29,570 --> 00:52:31,610
Mr. Potter.

625
00:52:33,370 --> 00:52:37,870
Our new celebrity.

626
00:52:39,250 --> 00:52:44,220
What would I get if I added root of asphodel to an infusion of wormwood?

627
00:52:48,180 --> 00:52:49,600
You don't know?

628
00:52:49,850 --> 00:52:50,810
Let's try again.

629
00:52:50,930 --> 00:52:54,600
Where would you look if I asked you to find a bezoar?

630
00:52:56,440 --> 00:52:58,400
I don't know, sir.

631
00:52:58,520 --> 00:53:01,650
What is the difference between monkshood and wolfsbane?

632
00:53:04,780 --> 00:53:06,280
I don't know, sir.

633
00:53:08,240 --> 00:53:10,040
Pity.

634
00:53:11,240 --> 00:53:16,080
Clearly, fame isn't everything...

635
00:53:16,170 --> 00:53:18,420
...is it, Mr. Potter?

636
00:53:21,210 --> 00:53:23,340
Eye of rabbit, harp string hum

637
00:53:23,470 --> 00:53:25,970
Turn this water into rum

638
00:53:27,890 --> 00:53:30,060
Eye of rabbit, harp string hum

639
00:53:30,180 --> 00:53:32,430
What's Seamus trying to do to the water?

640
00:53:32,520 --> 00:53:34,020
Turn it to rum.

641
00:53:34,140 --> 00:53:37,810
Actually managed a weak tea yesterday, before...

642
00:53:42,820 --> 00:53:45,820
Mail's here.

643
00:54:18,350 --> 00:54:19,980
Can I borrow this?

644
00:54:20,560 --> 00:54:21,480
Thanks.

645
00:54:24,900 --> 00:54:27,570
Look, Neville's got a Remembrall.

646
00:54:27,740 --> 00:54:29,200
I've read about those.

647
00:54:29,320 --> 00:54:30,950
The smoke turns red

648
00:54:31,070 --> 00:54:32,990
when you've forgotten something.

649
00:54:33,540 --> 00:54:34,950
The problem is,

650
00:54:35,080 --> 00:54:37,160
I can't remember what I've forgotten.

651
00:54:37,250 --> 00:54:38,370
Hey, Ron.

652
00:54:38,460 --> 00:54:40,630
Somebody broke into Gringotts.

653
00:54:40,750 --> 00:54:42,000
Listen.

654
00:54:42,090 --> 00:54:45,460
Believed to be the work of Dark wizards or witches...

655
00:54:45,590 --> 00:54:48,220
...Gringotts goblins acknowledge the breach

656
00:54:48,300 --> 00:54:50,090
but insist nothing was taken.

657
00:54:50,260 --> 00:54:52,390
The vault in question, number 713,

658
00:54:52,510 --> 00:54:56,140
had been emptied earlier that same day.

659
00:54:56,680 --> 00:54:57,850
That's odd.

660
00:54:57,930 --> 00:55:00,230
That's the vault Hagrid and I went to.

661
00:55:09,780 --> 00:55:11,110
Good afternoon, class.

662
00:55:11,200 --> 00:55:13,660
Good afternoon, Madam Hooch.

663
00:55:13,780 --> 00:55:15,660
Good afternoon, Amanda. Good afternoon.

664
00:55:17,790 --> 00:55:20,370
Welcome to your first flying lesson.

665
00:55:20,500 --> 00:55:21,960
What are you waiting for?

666
00:55:22,040 --> 00:55:24,630
Step up to your broomstick.

667
00:55:24,750 --> 00:55:26,340
Come on now, hurry up.

668
00:55:27,170 --> 00:55:29,130
Stick your hand over the broom

669
00:55:29,220 --> 00:55:30,340
and say, "Up."

670
00:55:30,470 --> 00:55:33,800
Up!

671
00:55:34,970 --> 00:55:36,890
Up.

672
00:55:37,970 --> 00:55:40,350
Up. Up!

673
00:55:40,480 --> 00:55:41,310
With feeling.

674
00:55:41,440 --> 00:55:47,980
Up. Up.

675
00:55:48,110 --> 00:55:49,110
Up!

676
00:55:50,990 --> 00:55:52,610
Shut up, Harry.

677
00:55:53,280 --> 00:55:56,370
Now, once you've got hold of your broom,

678
00:55:56,490 --> 00:56:00,250
I want you to mount it. Grip it tight.

679
00:56:00,370 --> 00:56:02,580
You don't wanna be sliding off the end.

680
00:56:02,670 --> 00:56:05,290
When I blow my whistle, I want you

681
00:56:05,420 --> 00:56:07,710
to kick off from the ground, hard.

682
00:56:07,840 --> 00:56:10,050
Keep your broom steady,

683
00:56:10,170 --> 00:56:11,800
hover for a moment...

684
00:56:11,880 --> 00:56:13,970
...then lean forward slightly

685
00:56:14,090 --> 00:56:15,550
and touch back down.

686
00:56:16,220 --> 00:56:19,930
On my whistle. Three, two...

687
00:56:21,940 --> 00:56:22,890
Mr. Longbottom.

688
00:56:24,690 --> 00:56:26,400
Neville!

689
00:56:27,980 --> 00:56:30,690
-Mr. Longbottom!   -Down, down!

690
00:56:30,780 --> 00:56:32,400
Neville!

691
00:56:36,030 --> 00:56:37,530
Come back down this instant!

692
00:56:37,660 --> 00:56:40,040
Oh, no!

693
00:56:44,960 --> 00:56:47,460
Help!

694
00:56:48,630 --> 00:56:49,710
Mr. Longbo...

695
00:56:53,090 --> 00:56:56,590
Help!

696
00:57:07,810 --> 00:57:09,480
Everyone out of the way!

697
00:57:15,280 --> 00:57:16,530
Is he all right?

698
00:57:16,620 --> 00:57:20,870
Oh, dear, it's a broken wrist.

699
00:57:21,160 --> 00:57:23,540
Poor boy. Come on now, up you get.

700
00:57:25,120 --> 00:57:28,000
Keep your feet on the ground

701
00:57:28,000 --> 00:57:30,000
while I take him to the hospital wing.

702
00:57:30,090 --> 00:57:31,250
Understand?

703
00:57:31,550 --> 00:57:33,880
If I see a single broom in the air...

704
00:57:33,970 --> 00:57:37,930
the one riding it will be expelled before they can say Quidditch.

705
00:57:39,430 --> 00:57:41,350
Did you see his face?

706
00:57:41,510 --> 00:57:43,730
If he had squeezed this,

707
00:57:43,850 --> 00:57:45,730
he'd have remembered to fall on his arse.

708
00:57:45,810 --> 00:57:47,310
Give it here, Malfoy.

709
00:57:48,810 --> 00:57:52,820
No. I'll leave it somewhere for Longbottom to find.

710
00:57:56,780 --> 00:57:58,200
How about on the roof?

711
00:58:00,530 --> 00:58:03,790
What's the matter, Potter? Bit beyond your reach?

712
00:58:06,500 --> 00:58:08,460
Harry, no way!

713
00:58:08,580 --> 00:58:10,040
You heard what Madam Hooch said.

714
00:58:10,130 --> 00:58:12,800
Besides, you don't know how to fly.

715
00:58:13,840 --> 00:58:15,760
What an idiot.

716
00:58:19,180 --> 00:58:20,430
Give it here, Malfoy

717
00:58:20,510 --> 00:58:22,310
or I'll knock you off your broom!

718
00:58:22,850 --> 00:58:24,220
Is that so?

719
00:58:27,940 --> 00:58:29,690
Have it your way, then.

720
00:59:01,850 --> 00:59:03,310
Nice going, Harry.

721
00:59:03,430 --> 00:59:04,510
That was wicked, Harry!

722
00:59:04,640 --> 00:59:06,140
Wicked, Harry!

723
00:59:07,800 --> 00:59:09,180
Harry Potter!

724
00:59:10,850 --> 00:59:12,100
Follow me.

725
00:59:24,570 --> 00:59:25,690
You wait here.

726
00:59:28,570 --> 00:59:30,110
Professor Quirrell, excuse me.

727
00:59:30,240 --> 00:59:33,490
Could I borrow Wood for a moment?

728
00:59:33,910 --> 00:59:36,200
Yes, of course.

729
00:59:41,290 --> 00:59:43,750
Potter, this is Oliver Wood.

730
00:59:43,960 --> 00:59:47,920
Wood, I have found you a Seeker.

731
00:59:49,430 --> 00:59:50,430
Have you heard?

732
00:59:50,550 --> 00:59:53,050
Harry Potter's the new Gryffindor Seeker.

733
00:59:53,180 --> 00:59:55,720
I always knew he'd do well.

734
00:59:55,810 --> 00:59:56,810
Seeker?

735
00:59:56,930 --> 00:59:59,850
But first yearsnever make the house teams.

736
00:59:59,940 --> 01:00:02,560
You must be the youngest player in...

737
01:00:02,560 --> 01:00:03,560
A century,

738
01:00:03,690 --> 01:00:04,650
McGonagall says.

739
01:00:04,770 --> 01:00:06,980
Well done, Harry. Wood's just told us.

740
01:00:07,610 --> 01:00:09,450
Fred and George are on the team.

741
01:00:09,570 --> 01:00:10,280
Beaters.

742
01:00:10,400 --> 01:00:11,320
Our job is

743
01:00:11,450 --> 01:00:14,120
to make sure you don't get bloodied up too bad.

744
01:00:14,240 --> 01:00:15,740
Can't make any promises.

745
01:00:15,830 --> 01:00:17,120
Rough game, Quidditch.

746
01:00:17,200 --> 01:00:19,500
But no one's died in years.

747
01:00:19,620 --> 01:00:21,170
Someone vanishes occasionally.

748
01:00:21,290 --> 01:00:23,630
But they'll turn up in a month or two.

749
01:00:24,210 --> 01:00:25,800
Go on, Harry.

750
01:00:25,920 --> 01:00:27,460
Quidditch is great.

751
01:00:27,590 --> 01:00:28,840
Best game there is,

752
01:00:28,960 --> 01:00:30,050
and you'll be great too.

753
01:00:30,170 --> 01:00:32,130
I've never played.

754
01:00:32,220 --> 01:00:33,510
What if I make a fool of myself?

755
01:00:33,640 --> 01:00:35,850
You won't make a fool of yourself.

756
01:00:35,970 --> 01:00:37,640
It's in your blood.

757
01:00:46,820 --> 01:00:49,900
You never told me your father was a Seeker too.

758
01:00:50,530 --> 01:00:52,990
I didn't know.

759
01:00:58,660 --> 01:01:01,210
I'm telling you, it's spooky.

760
01:01:01,330 --> 01:01:03,290
She knows more about you than you do.

761
01:01:03,370 --> 01:01:04,790
Who doesn't?

762
01:01:06,670 --> 01:01:08,090
What's happening?

763
01:01:08,920 --> 01:01:12,260
The staircases change, remember?

764
01:01:18,310 --> 01:01:19,350
Let's go this way.

765
01:01:19,470 --> 01:01:21,850
Before the staircase moves again.

766
01:01:30,690 --> 01:01:34,160
Does anybody feel like we shouldn't be here?

767
01:01:34,280 --> 01:01:36,450
We're not supposed to be here.

768
01:01:36,570 --> 01:01:39,660
This is the third floor. It's forbidden.

769
01:01:41,750 --> 01:01:43,040
Let's go.

770
01:01:45,420 --> 01:01:46,710
It's Filch's cat!

771
01:01:46,790 --> 01:01:47,790
Run!

772
01:01:52,130 --> 01:01:54,880
Quick, let's hide through that door!

773
01:02:00,560 --> 01:02:01,390
It's locked!

774
01:02:01,470 --> 01:02:02,850
We're done for!

775
01:02:02,930 --> 01:02:04,560
Move over!

776
01:02:06,060 --> 01:02:07,610
Alohomora.

777
01:02:09,150 --> 01:02:10,070
Get in.

778
01:02:12,230 --> 01:02:13,320
Alohomora?

779
01:02:13,440 --> 01:02:16,070
Standard Book of Spells, chapter seven.

780
01:02:16,160 --> 01:02:18,820
Anyone here, my sweet?

781
01:02:26,120 --> 01:02:27,290
Come on.

782
01:02:27,830 --> 01:02:28,790
Filch is gone.

783
01:02:28,920 --> 01:02:30,290
He thinks this door's locked.

784
01:02:30,380 --> 01:02:31,460
It was locked.

785
01:02:31,590 --> 01:02:33,340
And for good reason.

786
01:02:59,570 --> 01:03:01,370
What are they doing,

787
01:03:01,490 --> 01:03:05,120
keeping a thing like that locked up in a school?

788
01:03:05,370 --> 01:03:07,290
Didn't you see

789
01:03:07,370 --> 01:03:09,210
what it was standing on?

790
01:03:09,330 --> 01:03:11,170
I wasn't looking at its feet!

791
01:03:11,290 --> 01:03:13,630
I was preoccupied with its heads.

792
01:03:13,710 --> 01:03:16,670
Or maybe you didn't notice. There were three!

793
01:03:16,800 --> 01:03:18,300
It wasn't there by accident.

794
01:03:18,430 --> 01:03:20,550
It was standing on a trap door.

795
01:03:20,640 --> 01:03:22,430
It's guarding something.

796
01:03:23,060 --> 01:03:24,270
Guarding something?

797
01:03:24,350 --> 01:03:25,520
That's right.

798
01:03:25,640 --> 01:03:28,560
Now, if you two don't mind, I'm going to bed...

799
01:03:28,640 --> 01:03:30,980
...before you come up with another idea

800
01:03:31,060 --> 01:03:32,110
to get us killed.

801
01:03:32,230 --> 01:03:34,570
Or worse, expelled.

802
01:03:38,780 --> 01:03:42,160
She needs to sort out her priorities.

803
01:03:47,660 --> 01:03:50,250
Quidditch is easy to understand.

804
01:03:50,420 --> 01:03:52,000
Each team has seven players.

805
01:03:52,130 --> 01:03:54,210
Three Chasers, two Beaters,

806
01:03:54,340 --> 01:03:56,010
one keeper and a Seeker.

807
01:03:56,130 --> 01:03:57,170
That's you.

808
01:04:03,140 --> 01:04:04,850
There are three kinds of balls.

809
01:04:05,060 --> 01:04:06,720
This one's called the Quaffle.

810
01:04:07,220 --> 01:04:09,850
The Chasers handle the Quaffle

811
01:04:09,940 --> 01:04:12,650
and try to put it through one of those hoops.

812
01:04:13,400 --> 01:04:16,570
The keeper, that's me, defends the hoops.

813
01:04:16,730 --> 01:04:17,900
With me so far?

814
01:04:18,030 --> 01:04:19,150
I think so.

815
01:04:19,900 --> 01:04:21,410
What are those?

816
01:04:24,780 --> 01:04:26,080
You better take this.

817
01:04:37,210 --> 01:04:38,800
Careful now, it's coming back.

818
01:04:45,180 --> 01:04:47,520
Not bad, Potter.

819
01:04:48,850 --> 01:04:50,270
You'd make a fair Beater.

820
01:05:06,660 --> 01:05:08,040
What was that?

821
01:05:09,620 --> 01:05:10,960
Bludger.

822
01:05:11,370 --> 01:05:12,750
Nasty little buggers.

823
01:05:13,500 --> 01:05:14,960
But you...

824
01:05:15,080 --> 01:05:16,590
are a Seeker.

825
01:05:20,670 --> 01:05:24,840
The only thing I want you to worry about is this.

826
01:05:25,470 --> 01:05:27,260
The Golden Snitch.

827
01:05:28,510 --> 01:05:29,560
I like this ball.

828
01:05:29,680 --> 01:05:32,770
You like it now. Just wait.

829
01:05:32,890 --> 01:05:35,650
It's wicked fast and damn near impossible to see.

830
01:05:35,770 --> 01:05:37,730
What do I do with it?

831
01:05:37,860 --> 01:05:41,280
You catch it before the other team's Seeker.

832
01:05:41,360 --> 01:05:43,950
You catch this, the game's over.

833
01:05:44,110 --> 01:05:45,870
You catch this, Potter,

834
01:05:45,950 --> 01:05:47,580
and we win.

835
01:05:57,040 --> 01:06:02,590
One of a wizard's most rudimentary skills is levitation...

836
01:06:02,670 --> 01:06:04,680
...or the ability to make objects...

837
01:06:04,800 --> 01:06:05,970
...fly.

838
01:06:06,180 --> 01:06:08,140
Do you have your feathers?

839
01:06:08,260 --> 01:06:09,260
Good.

840
01:06:09,390 --> 01:06:10,640
Now,

841
01:06:10,720 --> 01:06:14,230
don't forget the nice wrist movement we've been practicing.

842
01:06:14,350 --> 01:06:17,020
The swish and flick.

843
01:06:17,150 --> 01:06:18,610
Everyone.

844
01:06:18,770 --> 01:06:21,530
The swish and flick.

845
01:06:21,900 --> 01:06:22,780
Good.

846
01:06:22,860 --> 01:06:24,990
and enunciate.

847
01:06:25,110 --> 01:06:27,740
Wingardium Leviosa.

848
01:06:27,820 --> 01:06:29,490
Off you go, then.

849
01:06:30,330 --> 01:06:33,040
Wingardium Leviosa.

850
01:06:33,160 --> 01:06:35,370
Wingardium Leviosa.

851
01:06:35,500 --> 01:06:38,540
Wingardium Leviosa.

852
01:06:39,210 --> 01:06:41,210
No, stop, stop, stop!

853
01:06:41,300 --> 01:06:43,630
You're going to take someone's eye out.

854
01:06:43,710 --> 01:06:46,010
Besides, you're saying it wrong.

855
01:06:46,130 --> 01:06:48,090
It's Leviosa,

856
01:06:48,220 --> 01:06:50,180
not Leviosar.

857
01:06:50,260 --> 01:06:53,640
You do it then, if you're so clever. Go on, go on.

858
01:06:55,810 --> 01:06:57,980
Wingardium Leviosa.

859
01:07:06,530 --> 01:07:08,530
Well done!

860
01:07:08,610 --> 01:07:11,780
See here, everyone, Miss Granger's done it!

861
01:07:11,870 --> 01:07:13,370
Splendid!

862
01:07:13,540 --> 01:07:15,500
Wingardium Leviosa...

863
01:07:15,580 --> 01:07:16,750
Well done, dear.

864
01:07:22,090 --> 01:07:25,340
I think we're going to need another feather over here.

865
01:07:32,430 --> 01:07:34,600
It's Leviosa,

866
01:07:34,720 --> 01:07:36,890
not Leviosar.

867
01:07:37,020 --> 01:07:39,020
She's a nightmare, honestly!

868
01:07:39,100 --> 01:07:41,400
No wonder she hasn't got any friends.

869
01:07:43,150 --> 01:07:44,610
I think she heard you.

870
01:08:14,260 --> 01:08:16,140
Where's Hermione?

871
01:08:16,270 --> 01:08:19,730
Parvati said she wouldn't come out of the bathroom.

872
01:08:19,810 --> 01:08:23,110
She said that she'd been in there all afternoon, crying.

873
01:08:28,490 --> 01:08:30,070
Troll

874
01:08:30,150 --> 01:08:32,110
in the dungeon!

875
01:08:32,200 --> 01:08:35,080
Troll in the dungeon!

876
01:08:38,450 --> 01:08:39,790
Thought you ought to know.

877
01:08:47,760 --> 01:08:50,760
Silence!

878
01:08:51,970 --> 01:08:55,350
Everyone will please not panic!

879
01:08:56,640 --> 01:08:58,140
Now...

880
01:08:58,430 --> 01:08:59,770
...prefects

881
01:08:59,850 --> 01:09:03,230
will lead their house back to the dormitories.

882
01:09:03,480 --> 01:09:07,860
Teachers will follow me to the dungeons.

883
01:09:19,620 --> 01:09:21,410
Gryffindors, keep up, please,

884
01:09:21,500 --> 01:09:23,080
and stay alert.

885
01:09:23,170 --> 01:09:24,580
How could a troll get in?

886
01:09:24,670 --> 01:09:25,960
Not on its own.

887
01:09:26,040 --> 01:09:29,710
Trolls are really stupid. Probably people playing jokes.

888
01:09:30,090 --> 01:09:30,920
What?

889
01:09:31,010 --> 01:09:33,180
Hermione! She doesn't know.

890
01:09:46,520 --> 01:09:48,860
I think the troll's left the dungeon.

891
01:09:53,900 --> 01:09:55,740
It's going into the girls' bathroom.

892
01:10:26,770 --> 01:10:28,400
Hermione, move!

893
01:10:32,700 --> 01:10:34,030
Help!

894
01:10:34,860 --> 01:10:36,410
Help!

895
01:10:38,700 --> 01:10:41,040
Hey, pea brain!

896
01:10:53,380 --> 01:10:54,680
Help!

897
01:11:16,280 --> 01:11:17,870
Do something!

898
01:11:19,990 --> 01:11:21,490
What?

899
01:11:21,830 --> 01:11:23,160
Anything!

900
01:11:24,750 --> 01:11:25,660
Hurry up!

901
01:11:25,790 --> 01:11:27,330
Swish and flick.

902
01:11:27,420 --> 01:11:29,840
Wingardium Leviosa.

903
01:11:40,640 --> 01:11:42,010
Cool.

904
01:12:07,080 --> 01:12:08,170
Is it...

905
01:12:08,250 --> 01:12:09,500
...dead?

906
01:12:09,830 --> 01:12:13,130
I don't think so. Just knocked out.

907
01:12:20,300 --> 01:12:21,850
Troll boogers.

908
01:12:24,850 --> 01:12:26,310
Oh, my goodness!

909
01:12:26,390 --> 01:12:28,770
Explain yourselves, both of you!

910
01:12:28,850 --> 01:12:33,400
-Well, what it is...   -It's my fault, Professor McGonagall.

911
01:12:33,400 --> 01:12:35,190
What?

912
01:12:35,530 --> 01:12:37,150
Miss Granger?

913
01:12:37,490 --> 01:12:39,360
I went looking for the troll.

914
01:12:39,450 --> 01:12:42,410
I thought I could handle it.

915
01:12:42,910 --> 01:12:44,740
But I was wrong.

916
01:12:45,040 --> 01:12:48,250
If Harry and Ron hadn't come and found me,

917
01:12:48,410 --> 01:12:50,420
I'd probably be dead.

918
01:12:51,080 --> 01:12:52,840
Be that as it may,

919
01:12:52,920 --> 01:12:55,630
it was an extremely foolish thing to do.

920
01:12:55,710 --> 01:12:58,840
I expected more rational behavior

921
01:12:58,970 --> 01:13:01,510
and am very disappointed in you.

922
01:13:01,640 --> 01:13:04,720
Five points will be taken from Gryffindor...

923
01:13:04,890 --> 01:13:07,850
...for your serious lack of judgment.

924
01:13:08,810 --> 01:13:10,940
As for you two gentlemen...

925
01:13:11,020 --> 01:13:14,310
...I just hope you realize how fortunate you are.

926
01:13:14,690 --> 01:13:18,190
Not many first-year students could take on a troll...

927
01:13:18,280 --> 01:13:21,030
...and live to tell the tale.

928
01:13:21,200 --> 01:13:24,160
Five points...

929
01:13:25,030 --> 01:13:27,950
...will be awarded to each of you...

930
01:13:29,750 --> 01:13:32,540
...for sheer dumb luck.

931
01:13:37,420 --> 01:13:39,630
Perhaps you ought to go.

932
01:13:39,760 --> 01:13:41,130
It might wake up.

933
01:13:50,060 --> 01:13:52,310
Take a bit of toast, mate. Go on.

934
01:13:52,850 --> 01:13:54,020
Ron's right, Harry.

935
01:13:54,150 --> 01:13:56,150
You'll need your strength today.

936
01:13:56,400 --> 01:13:57,900
I'm not hungry.

937
01:13:59,230 --> 01:14:00,780
Good luck today, Potter.

938
01:14:02,450 --> 01:14:05,370
But another you've proven yourself against a troll.

939
01:14:05,490 --> 01:14:07,530
A game of Quidditch should be easy work.

940
01:14:08,330 --> 01:14:11,830
Even if it is against Slytherin.

941
01:14:19,210 --> 01:14:21,010
That explains the blood.

942
01:14:21,670 --> 01:14:23,050
Blood?

943
01:14:23,130 --> 01:14:26,260
Last night, I'm guessing Snape...

944
01:14:26,390 --> 01:14:27,930
...let the troll in as a diversion...

945
01:14:28,010 --> 01:14:29,970
...so he could get past that dog.

946
01:14:30,100 --> 01:14:31,930
But he got bit,

947
01:14:32,020 --> 01:14:33,060
that's why he's limping.

948
01:14:33,190 --> 01:14:35,980
But why would anyone go near that dog?

949
01:14:36,060 --> 01:14:37,730
At Gringotts,

950
01:14:37,820 --> 01:14:39,400
Hagrid took something out of the vault.

951
01:14:39,530 --> 01:14:42,490
Said it was Hogwarts business, very secret.

952
01:14:42,820 --> 01:14:44,320
You're saying...

953
01:14:44,450 --> 01:14:46,120
That's what the dog's guarding.

954
01:14:46,240 --> 01:14:47,950
That's what Snape wants.

955
01:15:02,010 --> 01:15:03,880
Bit early for mail, isn't it?

956
01:15:04,010 --> 01:15:06,300
But I never get mail.

957
01:15:06,590 --> 01:15:08,140
Let's open it.

958
01:15:18,310 --> 01:15:20,110
It's a broomstick.

959
01:15:20,230 --> 01:15:22,690
That's not just a broomstick,

960
01:15:22,780 --> 01:15:24,860
it's a Nimbus 2000!

961
01:15:26,280 --> 01:15:27,950
But who...?

962
01:15:49,510 --> 01:15:50,760
Scared, Harry?

963
01:15:51,100 --> 01:15:52,310
A little.

964
01:15:52,430 --> 01:15:53,680
It's all right.

965
01:15:53,850 --> 01:15:55,890
I felt the same way before my first game.

966
01:15:56,100 --> 01:15:57,100
What happened?

967
01:15:57,230 --> 01:15:59,730
I don't really remember.

968
01:15:59,940 --> 01:16:02,650
I took a Bludger to the head two minutes in.

969
01:16:02,730 --> 01:16:04,900
Woke up in hospital a week later.

970
01:16:27,880 --> 01:16:29,470
Welcome to Hogwarts'

971
01:16:29,590 --> 01:16:31,260
first Quidditch game of the season.

972
01:16:31,350 --> 01:16:34,930
Today's game, Slytherin versus Gryffindor!

973
01:16:40,940 --> 01:16:42,940
Gryffindor!

974
01:17:06,550 --> 01:17:08,420
The players take their positions...

975
01:17:08,550 --> 01:17:12,220
...as Madam Hooch steps onto the field to begin the game!

976
01:17:13,050 --> 01:17:16,270
Now, I want a nice, clean game...

977
01:17:17,020 --> 01:17:19,020
...from all of you!

978
01:17:24,900 --> 01:17:27,650
The Bludgers are up, followed by the Golden Snitch.

979
01:17:27,740 --> 01:17:30,530
Remember, the Snitch is worth 150 points.

980
01:17:30,650 --> 01:17:33,620
The Seeker who catches the Snitch ends the game.

981
01:17:40,660 --> 01:17:42,330
The Quaffle is released

982
01:17:42,670 --> 01:17:44,080
and the game begins!

983
01:18:03,310 --> 01:18:05,150
Angelina Johnson scores!

984
01:18:05,270 --> 01:18:07,020
Ten points for Gryffindor!

985
01:18:10,690 --> 01:18:11,820
Yes!

986
01:18:13,490 --> 01:18:14,700
Well done!

987
01:18:19,200 --> 01:18:21,160
Slytherin takes the Quaffle.

988
01:18:21,290 --> 01:18:23,500
Bletchley passes to Captain Marcus Flint.

989
01:18:55,860 --> 01:18:56,740
Yes!

990
01:18:56,820 --> 01:18:59,200
Another 10 points to Gryffindor!

991
01:19:13,550 --> 01:19:14,550
Give me that!

992
01:19:46,710 --> 01:19:48,210
Take that side!

993
01:20:38,720 --> 01:20:40,840
What's going on with Harry's broomstick?

994
01:20:51,060 --> 01:20:53,270
It's Snape. He's jinxing the broom!

995
01:20:53,400 --> 01:20:55,570
Jinxing the broom? What do we do?

996
01:20:55,690 --> 01:20:56,690
Leave it to me.

997
01:21:19,720 --> 01:21:21,090
Come on, Hermione!

998
01:21:35,190 --> 01:21:37,740
Lacarnum Inflamarae.

999
01:21:46,080 --> 01:21:47,240
Fire!

1000
01:21:47,370 --> 01:21:48,620
You're on fire!

1001
01:22:06,970 --> 01:22:09,310
Go, go, go, go!

1002
01:23:01,070 --> 01:23:02,490
Looks like he's gonna be sick.

1003
01:23:04,860 --> 01:23:06,160
He's got the Snitch!

1004
01:23:06,280 --> 01:23:09,540
Harry Potter receives 150 points for catching the Snitch!

1005
01:23:10,450 --> 01:23:12,080
Gryffindor wins!

1006
01:23:16,000 --> 01:23:17,170
No

1007
01:23:21,090 --> 01:23:22,380
Yeah!

1008
01:23:55,750 --> 01:23:57,330
Nonsense!

1009
01:23:57,420 --> 01:24:00,090
Why would Snape put a curse on Harry's broom?

1010
01:24:00,210 --> 01:24:01,050
Who knows?

1011
01:24:01,170 --> 01:24:04,210
Why was he trying to get past that three-headed dog in Hallowmas?

1012
01:24:04,470 --> 01:24:05,840
Who told you about Fluffy?

1013
01:24:05,970 --> 01:24:06,840
Fluffy?

1014
01:24:06,930 --> 01:24:08,720
That thing has a name?

1015
01:24:08,840 --> 01:24:10,760
Of course he has a name. He's mine.

1016
01:24:10,890 --> 01:24:13,720
I bought him off an Irishman in pub last year.

1017
01:24:14,020 --> 01:24:16,230
-I lent him to Dumbledore to guard...  -Yes?

1018
01:24:16,310 --> 01:24:18,520
Shouldn't have said that. No more questions!

1019
01:24:18,650 --> 01:24:21,150
No more questions! That's top-secret.

1020
01:24:21,270 --> 01:24:22,480
But Hagrid...

1021
01:24:22,570 --> 01:24:25,690
whatever Fluffy's guarding, Snape's trying to steal it.

1022
01:24:25,780 --> 01:24:27,240
Codswallop.

1023
01:24:27,360 --> 01:24:29,530
Professor Snape is a Hogwarts teacher.

1024
01:24:29,570 --> 01:24:31,450
Hogwarts teacher or not,

1025
01:24:31,530 --> 01:24:33,490
I know a spell when I see one.

1026
01:24:33,620 --> 01:24:35,200
I've read all about them.

1027
01:24:35,290 --> 01:24:36,660
You've got to keep eye contact,

1028
01:24:36,790 --> 01:24:38,830
Snape wasn't blinking

1029
01:24:38,960 --> 01:24:40,330
Exactly.

1030
01:24:41,500 --> 01:24:44,550
Now, you listen to me, all three of you.

1031
01:24:44,670 --> 01:24:47,630
You're meddling in things that ought not to be meddled in.

1032
01:24:47,880 --> 01:24:49,430
It's dangerous.

1033
01:24:49,510 --> 01:24:50,970
What that dog is guarding is

1034
01:24:51,050 --> 01:24:54,720
between Dumbledore and Nicholas Flamel.

1035
01:24:54,810 --> 01:24:56,680
Nicholas Flamel?

1036
01:24:57,310 --> 01:24:58,770
I shouldn't have said that.

1037
01:24:58,850 --> 01:25:01,980
I should not have said that.

1038
01:25:02,110 --> 01:25:03,480
Nicholas Flamel.

1039
01:25:04,440 --> 01:25:06,360
Who's Nicholas Flamel?

1040
01:25:06,530 --> 01:25:07,990
I don't know.

1041
01:25:53,200 --> 01:25:55,580
knight to E-5.

1042
01:26:04,090 --> 01:26:06,050
Queen to E-5.

1043
01:26:11,810 --> 01:26:13,680
That's totally barbaric!

1044
01:26:13,770 --> 01:26:15,890
That's wizard's chess.

1045
01:26:16,440 --> 01:26:17,520
I see you've packed.

1046
01:26:17,640 --> 01:26:19,100
I see you haven't.

1047
01:26:19,230 --> 01:26:21,060
Change of plans. My parents...

1048
01:26:21,190 --> 01:26:24,360
went to Romania to visit my brother Charlie.

1049
01:26:24,740 --> 01:26:26,280
He's studying dragons there.

1050
01:26:26,400 --> 01:26:28,860
Good. You can help Harry.

1051
01:26:28,910 --> 01:26:32,660
He's going to the library to look up Nicholas Flamel.

1052
01:26:32,740 --> 01:26:35,330
We've looked a hundred times!

1053
01:26:36,660 --> 01:26:39,000
Not in the restricted section.

1054
01:26:39,540 --> 01:26:40,750
Happy Christmas.

1055
01:26:44,000 --> 01:26:46,880
I think we've had a bad influence on her.

1056
01:26:49,470 --> 01:26:51,050
Harry, wake up!

1057
01:26:51,260 --> 01:26:52,850
Come on, Harry, wake up!

1058
01:27:03,770 --> 01:27:04,900
Happy Christmas, Harry.

1059
01:27:04,980 --> 01:27:06,440
Happy Christmas, Ron.

1060
01:27:07,280 --> 01:27:09,070
What are you wearing?

1061
01:27:10,070 --> 01:27:12,240
my mum made it.

1062
01:27:12,410 --> 01:27:13,910
Looks like you've got one too.

1063
01:27:14,030 --> 01:27:16,330
I've got presents?

1064
01:27:16,410 --> 01:27:17,580
Yeah.

1065
01:27:24,800 --> 01:27:26,090
There they are.

1066
01:27:38,140 --> 01:27:41,310
Your father left this in my possession before he died.

1067
01:27:41,440 --> 01:27:44,020
It is time it was returned to you.

1068
01:27:44,060 --> 01:27:45,610
Use it well.

1069
01:28:02,620 --> 01:28:03,960
What is it?

1070
01:28:04,210 --> 01:28:06,420
Some kind of cloak.

1071
01:28:06,500 --> 01:28:08,590
Well, let's see, then. Put it on.

1072
01:28:15,050 --> 01:28:16,260
My body's gone!

1073
01:28:16,390 --> 01:28:20,520
I know what that is. That's an invisibility cloak!

1074
01:28:20,640 --> 01:28:22,020
I'm invisible?

1075
01:28:22,850 --> 01:28:24,480
They're really rare.

1076
01:28:26,230 --> 01:28:27,730
I wonder who gave it to you.

1077
01:28:27,820 --> 01:28:29,190
There was no name.

1078
01:28:29,440 --> 01:28:31,150
It just said,

1079
01:28:31,360 --> 01:28:32,200
Use it well.

1080
01:29:00,770 --> 01:29:03,100
Famous Fire-Eaters.

1081
01:29:03,140 --> 01:29:06,150
Fifteenth-Century Fiends.

1082
01:29:06,730 --> 01:29:08,360
Flamel.

1083
01:29:08,480 --> 01:29:09,730
Nicholas Flamel.

1084
01:29:10,110 --> 01:29:11,360
Where are you?

1085
01:29:31,420 --> 01:29:32,630
Who's there?

1086
01:29:39,560 --> 01:29:41,060
I know you're in there.

1087
01:29:42,220 --> 01:29:43,980
You can't hide.

1088
01:29:52,530 --> 01:29:53,740
Who is it?

1089
01:29:54,030 --> 01:29:55,360
Show yourself.

1090
01:30:43,370 --> 01:30:45,580
Severus, I...

1091
01:30:45,660 --> 01:30:49,210
You don't want me as your enemy, Quirrell.

1092
01:30:49,580 --> 01:30:51,540
I don't know what you mean.

1093
01:30:51,630 --> 01:30:53,420
You know perfectly well what I mean.

1094
01:31:11,610 --> 01:31:14,440
We'll have another little chat soon.

1095
01:31:14,780 --> 01:31:19,570
When you've had time to decide where your loyalties lie.

1096
01:31:19,860 --> 01:31:21,570
Professors.

1097
01:31:21,700 --> 01:31:25,540
I found this in the restricted section.

1098
01:31:25,660 --> 01:31:27,200
It's still hot.

1099
01:31:27,330 --> 01:31:29,960
That means there's a student out of bed.

1100
01:33:02,760 --> 01:33:05,160
Mum?

1101
01:33:07,850 --> 01:33:10,420
Dad?

1102
01:33:44,420 --> 01:33:46,680
Ron, you've really gotta see this!

1103
01:33:46,680 --> 01:33:48,100
Ron, you've gotta see this!

1104
01:33:51,270 --> 01:33:54,520
Ron, come on, get out of bed!

1105
01:33:54,520 --> 01:33:55,310
Why?

1106
01:33:55,440 --> 01:33:58,060
There's something you've got to see!

1107
01:34:04,740 --> 01:34:06,240
Come on! Come!

1108
01:34:06,360 --> 01:34:07,820
Come look, it's my parents!

1109
01:34:10,450 --> 01:34:12,660
I only see us.

1110
01:34:12,660 --> 01:34:15,710
Look in properly. Go on, stand there.

1111
01:34:16,170 --> 01:34:18,380
There. You see them, don't you?

1112
01:34:18,500 --> 01:34:22,590
That's me! Only I'm head boy.

1113
01:34:22,670 --> 01:34:25,600
And I'm holding the Quidditch Cup.

1114
01:34:25,810 --> 01:34:28,010
And bloody hell!

1115
01:34:28,010 --> 01:34:30,100
I'm Quidditch captain too!

1116
01:34:30,390 --> 01:34:32,720
I look good.

1117
01:34:33,600 --> 01:34:37,600
Harry, do you think this mirror shows the future?

1118
01:34:37,600 --> 01:34:39,610
How can it?

1119
01:34:39,610 --> 01:34:43,250
Both my parents are dead.

1120
01:35:06,350 --> 01:35:08,510
Back again, Harry?

1121
01:35:11,010 --> 01:35:13,720
I see that you, like many before you...

1122
01:35:13,810 --> 01:35:17,270
...have discovered the delights of the Mirror of Erised.

1123
01:35:18,230 --> 01:35:22,440
I trust by now you realize what it does.

1124
01:35:23,730 --> 01:35:25,820
Let me give you a clue.

1125
01:35:26,780 --> 01:35:29,110
The happiest man on earth...

1126
01:35:29,240 --> 01:35:35,670
...would look in the mirror and see only himself exactly as he is.

1127
01:35:35,670 --> 01:35:38,830
So then, it shows us what we want.

1128
01:35:38,960 --> 01:35:40,500
Whatever we want.

1129
01:35:40,620 --> 01:35:42,080
Yes.

1130
01:35:42,170 --> 01:35:43,790
And no.

1131
01:35:44,250 --> 01:35:47,010
It shows us nothing more or less...

1132
01:35:47,130 --> 01:35:52,510
...than the deepest and most desperate desires of our hearts.

1133
01:35:53,180 --> 01:35:58,020
Now you, Harry, who have never known your family...

1134
01:35:58,020 --> 01:36:02,230
...you see them standing beside you.

1135
01:36:02,230 --> 01:36:04,900
But remember this, Harry.

1136
01:36:04,900 --> 01:36:07,110
This mirror

1137
01:36:07,110 --> 01:36:12,700
gives us neither knowledge or truth.

1138
01:36:13,950 --> 01:36:17,450
Men have wasted away in front of it.

1139
01:36:17,450 --> 01:36:19,500
Even gone mad.

1140
01:36:21,000 --> 01:36:25,420
That is why tomorrow, it will be moved to a new home.

1141
01:36:25,420 --> 01:36:28,010
And I must ask you...

1142
01:36:28,090 --> 01:36:32,800
...not to go looking for it again.

1143
01:36:32,890 --> 01:36:36,660
It does not do to dwell on dreams...

1144
01:36:36,720 --> 01:36:38,500
...and forget to live.

1145
01:37:34,150 --> 01:37:36,450
I had you looking in the wrong section.

1146
01:37:36,450 --> 01:37:39,080
How could I be so stupid?

1147
01:37:39,990 --> 01:37:43,500
I checked this out weeks ago for a bit of light reading.

1148
01:37:43,500 --> 01:37:46,030
This is light?

1149
01:37:50,500 --> 01:37:52,630
Of course! Here it is!

1150
01:37:52,760 --> 01:37:55,170
Nicholas Flamel is the

1151
01:37:55,170 --> 01:37:57,220
only known maker of the Sorcerer's Stone.

1152
01:37:57,220 --> 01:37:58,720
The what?

1153
01:37:58,800 --> 01:38:01,970
Honestly, don't you two read?

1154
01:38:01,970 --> 01:38:04,770
The Sorcerer's Stone is a legendarysubstance

1155
01:38:04,770 --> 01:38:06,770
with astonishing powers.

1156
01:38:06,900 --> 01:38:09,310
It'll transform any metal into pure gold...

1157
01:38:09,440 --> 01:38:11,690
...and produces the Elixir of Life which

1158
01:38:11,690 --> 01:38:13,610
will make the drinker immortal.

1159
01:38:13,690 --> 01:38:14,700
Immortal?

1160
01:38:14,820 --> 01:38:15,860
It means you'll never die.

1161
01:38:15,950 --> 01:38:17,870
I know what it means!

1162
01:38:18,910 --> 01:38:21,580
The only Stone currently in existence

1163
01:38:21,700 --> 01:38:23,870
belongs to Mr. Nicholas Flamel...

1164
01:38:23,950 --> 01:38:25,620
...the noted alchemist

1165
01:38:25,710 --> 01:38:30,130
who last year celebrated his 665th birthday.

1166
01:38:30,710 --> 01:38:33,130
That's what Fluffy's guarding.

1167
01:38:33,210 --> 01:38:38,560
That's what's under the trap door. The Sorcerer's Stone.

1168
01:38:54,230 --> 01:38:55,360
Hagrid, hello.

1169
01:38:55,490 --> 01:38:56,610
Don't wish to be rude,

1170
01:38:56,740 --> 01:38:58,530
but I'm in no state to entertain.

1171
01:38:58,610 --> 01:39:02,080
We know about the Sorcerer's Stone.

1172
01:39:06,290 --> 01:39:07,710
We think Snape's trying to steal it.

1173
01:39:07,790 --> 01:39:08,870
Snape?

1174
01:39:09,000 --> 01:39:11,210
Are you still on about him?

1175
01:39:11,420 --> 01:39:13,170
We know he's after it.

1176
01:39:13,250 --> 01:39:14,630
We don't know why.

1177
01:39:14,710 --> 01:39:16,050
Snape is...

1178
01:39:16,130 --> 01:39:17,590
one of the teachers protecting the Stone.

1179
01:39:17,800 --> 01:39:19,840
-He won't steal it.   -What?

1180
01:39:19,970 --> 01:39:21,390
You heard.

1181
01:39:21,470 --> 01:39:24,010
Come on, I'm a bit preoccupied today.

1182
01:39:24,100 --> 01:39:26,810
Wait a minute. One of the teachers?

1183
01:39:26,810 --> 01:39:31,150
Of course. There are other things defending the Stone, aren't there?

1184
01:39:31,150 --> 01:39:32,860
Spells, enchantments.

1185
01:39:32,980 --> 01:39:37,190
Right. Waste of bloody time, if you ask me.

1186
01:39:37,190 --> 01:39:39,440
Ain't no one gonna get past Fluffy.

1187
01:39:39,440 --> 01:39:43,230
Ain't a soul knows how, except for me and Dumbledore.

1188
01:39:43,310 --> 01:39:43,860
I shouldn't have told you that.

1189
01:39:43,860 --> 01:39:47,450
I shouldn't have told you that.

1190
01:40:00,080 --> 01:40:03,130
Hagrid, what exactly is that?

1191
01:40:03,130 --> 01:40:04,840
That? It's...

1192
01:40:04,920 --> 01:40:05,880
It's...

1193
01:40:06,000 --> 01:40:08,380
I know what that is!

1194
01:40:08,380 --> 01:40:11,090
But, Hagrid, how did you get one?

1195
01:40:11,180 --> 01:40:14,720
I won it. Off a stranger I met down at the pub.

1196
01:40:14,720 --> 01:40:18,180
Seemed quite glad to be rid of it, as a matter of fact.

1197
01:40:41,120 --> 01:40:43,880
Is that...

1198
01:40:44,170 --> 01:40:45,580
...a dragon?

1199
01:40:45,710 --> 01:40:50,050
That's not just a dragon. That's a Norwegian Ridgeback.

1200
01:40:50,170 --> 01:40:53,130
My brother works with these in Romania.

1201
01:40:53,220 --> 01:40:54,840
Isn't he beautiful?

1202
01:40:54,970 --> 01:40:57,300
Oh, bless him. Look, he knows his mummy.

1203
01:40:58,680 --> 01:41:00,810
Hello, Norbert.

1204
01:41:00,810 --> 01:41:02,060
Norbert?

1205
01:41:02,060 --> 01:41:04,560
He's gotta have a name, don't he?

1206
01:41:05,860 --> 01:41:08,020
Don't you, Norbert?

1207
01:41:15,360 --> 01:41:17,450
He'll have to be trained up a bit, of course.

1208
01:41:22,250 --> 01:41:24,880
Who's that?

1209
01:41:26,040 --> 01:41:28,750
Malfoy.

1210
01:41:28,920 --> 01:41:30,900
Oh, dear.

1211
01:41:32,170 --> 01:41:34,220
Hagrid always wanted a dragon.

1212
01:41:34,380 --> 01:41:36,590
Told me so the first time I met him.

1213
01:41:37,050 --> 01:41:39,010
It's crazy.

1214
01:41:39,010 --> 01:41:41,310
And worse, Malfoy knows.

1215
01:41:41,430 --> 01:41:43,430
I don't understand. Is that bad?

1216
01:41:43,520 --> 01:41:45,020
It's bad.

1217
01:41:45,690 --> 01:41:48,410
Good evening.

1218
01:41:51,480 --> 01:41:54,570
Nothing, I repeat, nothing...

1219
01:41:54,570 --> 01:41:58,410
...gives a student the right to walk about at night.

1220
01:41:58,410 --> 01:42:01,200
Therefore, as punishment for your actions,

1221
01:42:01,200 --> 01:42:03,330
50 points will be taken.

1222
01:42:03,410 --> 01:42:04,830
50?!

1223
01:42:04,830 --> 01:42:06,420
Each.

1224
01:42:06,830 --> 01:42:09,420
To ensure it doesn't happen again...

1225
01:42:09,420 --> 01:42:13,270
...all four of you will receive detention.

1226
01:42:13,670 --> 01:42:15,090
Excuse me, professor,

1227
01:42:15,090 --> 01:42:16,630
perhaps I heard you wrong.

1228
01:42:16,720 --> 01:42:19,300
I thought you said the four of us.

1229
01:42:19,300 --> 01:42:22,140
No, you heard me correctly.

1230
01:42:22,140 --> 01:42:24,310
Honorable as your intentions were,

1231
01:42:24,430 --> 01:42:27,480
you too were out of bed after hours.

1232
01:42:27,600 --> 01:42:31,110
You will join your classmates in detention.

1233
01:42:41,830 --> 01:42:44,950
A pity they let the old punishments die.

1234
01:42:45,580 --> 01:42:50,540
Was a time detention found you hanging by your thumbs in the dungeons.

1235
01:42:50,540 --> 01:42:54,280
God, I miss the screaming.

1236
01:42:56,300 --> 01:42:59,680
You'll be serving detention with Hagrid tonight.

1237
01:42:59,680 --> 01:43:01,970
He's got a little job to do

1238
01:43:01,970 --> 01:43:04,350
inside the Dark Forest.

1239
01:43:07,180 --> 01:43:10,700
A sorry lot, this, Hagrid.

1240
01:43:11,810 --> 01:43:12,900
Good God,

1241
01:43:13,020 --> 01:43:15,860
you're not still on about that bloody dragon, are you?

1242
01:43:18,950 --> 01:43:20,200
Norbert's gone.

1243
01:43:21,410 --> 01:43:24,040
Dumbledore sent him off to Romania

1244
01:43:24,040 --> 01:43:25,240
to live in a colony.

1245
01:43:25,330 --> 01:43:26,910
That's good, isn't it?

1246
01:43:26,910 --> 01:43:28,710
He's with his own kind.

1247
01:43:28,830 --> 01:43:31,170
What if he don't like Romania?

1248
01:43:31,290 --> 01:43:34,050
What if the other dragons are mean to him?

1249
01:43:34,050 --> 01:43:36,090
He's only a baby.

1250
01:43:36,170 --> 01:43:38,840
For God's sake, pull yourself together.

1251
01:43:38,840 --> 01:43:41,590
You're going into the Forest.

1252
01:43:41,720 --> 01:43:44,260
Got to have your wits about you.

1253
01:43:44,260 --> 01:43:47,180
The Forest? I thought that was a joke.

1254
01:43:47,180 --> 01:43:49,350
We can't go in there.

1255
01:43:50,270 --> 01:43:52,400
Students aren't allowed.

1256
01:43:52,400 --> 01:43:54,400
And there are...

1257
01:43:55,730 --> 01:43:57,490
...werewolves.

1258
01:43:57,490 --> 01:44:00,780
There's more than werewolves in those trees.

1259
01:44:00,910 --> 01:44:04,150
You can be sure of that.

1260
01:44:05,660 --> 01:44:07,200
Nighty-night.

1261
01:44:09,790 --> 01:44:11,040
Right.

1262
01:44:11,580 --> 01:44:12,710
Let's go.

1263
01:44:50,660 --> 01:44:52,920
Hagrid, what is that?

1264
01:44:52,920 --> 01:44:54,920
What we're here for.

1265
01:44:54,920 --> 01:44:56,340
See that?

1266
01:44:57,000 --> 01:44:59,960
That's unicorn blood, that is.

1267
01:44:59,960 --> 01:45:02,760
I found one dead a few weeks ago.

1268
01:45:02,930 --> 01:45:03,580
Now,

1269
01:45:03,580 --> 01:45:08,140
this one's been hurt bad by something.

1270
01:45:15,230 --> 01:45:16,810
So,

1271
01:45:16,980 --> 01:45:19,360
it's our job...

1272
01:45:19,480 --> 01:45:21,150
to go and find the poor beast.

1273
01:45:21,240 --> 01:45:23,320
Ron, Hermione, come with me.

1274
01:45:24,700 --> 01:45:28,530
And, Harry, you'll go with Malfoy.

1275
01:45:29,410 --> 01:45:31,620
Okay. Then I get Fang.

1276
01:45:31,750 --> 01:45:33,210
Fine.

1277
01:45:33,290 --> 01:45:36,710
Just so you know, he's a bloody coward.

1278
01:45:41,210 --> 01:45:43,760
Wait till my father hears about this.

1279
01:45:43,880 --> 01:45:46,090
This is servant's stuff.

1280
01:45:46,340 --> 01:45:48,350
If I didn't know better,

1281
01:45:48,430 --> 01:45:50,060
I'd say you were scared.

1282
01:45:50,180 --> 01:45:53,890
I'm not scared, Potter.

1283
01:45:54,190 --> 01:45:56,700
Do you hear that?

1284
01:45:58,610 --> 01:46:00,520
Come on, Fang.

1285
01:46:00,520 --> 01:46:01,820
Scared!

1286
01:46:26,970 --> 01:46:28,140
What is it, Fang?

1287
01:46:45,190 --> 01:46:47,150
Help!

1288
01:47:39,420 --> 01:47:42,960
Harry Potter, you must leave.

1289
01:47:42,960 --> 01:47:45,050
You are known to many creatures here.

1290
01:47:45,170 --> 01:47:47,800
The Forest is not safe at this time.

1291
01:47:47,880 --> 01:47:49,430
Especially for you.

1292
01:47:49,550 --> 01:47:52,090
What was that thing you saved me from?

1293
01:47:52,220 --> 01:47:54,890
A monstrous creature.

1294
01:47:54,890 --> 01:47:57,810
It is a terrible crime to slay a unicorn.

1295
01:47:57,930 --> 01:48:01,100
Drinking its blood will keep you alive

1296
01:48:01,190 --> 01:48:03,520
even if you are an inch from death.

1297
01:48:03,650 --> 01:48:05,730
But at a terrible price.

1298
01:48:05,860 --> 01:48:08,860
For you have slain something so pure...

1299
01:48:08,990 --> 01:48:11,820
...that the moment the blood touches your lips,

1300
01:48:11,950 --> 01:48:14,160
you will have a half-life.

1301
01:48:14,240 --> 01:48:15,990
A cursed life.

1302
01:48:16,080 --> 01:48:17,870
Who would choose such a life?

1303
01:48:17,950 --> 01:48:19,870
Can you think of no one?

1304
01:48:20,040 --> 01:48:22,540
Do you mean to say that

1305
01:48:22,540 --> 01:48:25,340
that thing that killed the unicorn...

1306
01:48:25,460 --> 01:48:27,880
...that was drinking its blood,

1307
01:48:27,960 --> 01:48:29,510
that was Voldemort?

1308
01:48:29,630 --> 01:48:33,930
Do you know what is hidden in the school at this very moment?

1309
01:48:35,550 --> 01:48:37,580
The Sorcerer's Stone.

1310
01:48:38,560 --> 01:48:39,810
Harry!

1311
01:48:40,890 --> 01:48:42,650
Hello there, Firenze.

1312
01:48:42,650 --> 01:48:44,770
See you've met our young Mr. Potter.

1313
01:48:45,650 --> 01:48:48,330
You all right there, Harry?

1314
01:48:49,070 --> 01:48:50,820
Harry Potter,

1315
01:48:50,900 --> 01:48:53,030
this is where I leave you.

1316
01:48:54,120 --> 01:48:56,530
You're safe now.

1317
01:48:56,530 --> 01:48:57,990
Good luck.

1318
01:49:05,420 --> 01:49:09,090
You mean, You-Iknow-Who is out there right now

1319
01:49:09,090 --> 01:49:09,920
in the Forest?

1320
01:49:10,050 --> 01:49:10,970
But he's weak.

1321
01:49:11,090 --> 01:49:12,970
He's living off the unicorns.

1322
01:49:13,090 --> 01:49:14,180
Don't you see?

1323
01:49:14,300 --> 01:49:15,760
We had it wrong.

1324
01:49:15,850 --> 01:49:18,390
Snape doesn't want the Stone for himself.

1325
01:49:18,390 --> 01:49:20,390
He wants it for Voldemort.

1326
01:49:20,560 --> 01:49:21,930
With the Elixir of Life,

1327
01:49:21,930 --> 01:49:23,600
Voldemort will be strong again.

1328
01:49:23,730 --> 01:49:27,310
He'll come back.

1329
01:49:27,310 --> 01:49:28,900
But if he comes back...

1330
01:49:29,030 --> 01:49:33,700
...you don't think he'll try to kill you, do you?

1331
01:49:34,110 --> 01:49:38,030
If he'd had the chance, he might have tried tonight.

1332
01:49:38,030 --> 01:49:41,910
And to think I've been worrying about my Potions final.

1333
01:49:41,950 --> 01:49:45,710
Hang on a minute. We're forgetting one thing.

1334
01:49:45,790 --> 01:49:49,750
Who's the one wizard Voldemort always feared?

1335
01:49:51,300 --> 01:49:51,870
Dumbledore.

1336
01:49:51,870 --> 01:49:56,590
As long as Dumbledore is around, Harry, you're safe.

1337
01:49:56,590 --> 01:49:58,470
As long as Dumbledore is around,

1338
01:49:58,470 --> 01:50:00,470
you can't be touched.

1339
01:50:06,400 --> 01:50:07,860
I'd heard

1340
01:50:07,860 --> 01:50:09,900
Hogwarts' final exams were frightful,

1341
01:50:10,020 --> 01:50:12,230
but I found that enjoyable.

1342
01:50:12,320 --> 01:50:13,860
Speak for yourself.

1343
01:50:13,940 --> 01:50:15,490
All right there, Harry?

1344
01:50:15,990 --> 01:50:17,780
My scar.

1345
01:50:17,780 --> 01:50:19,370
It keeps burning.

1346
01:50:19,910 --> 01:50:21,490
It's happened before.

1347
01:50:21,580 --> 01:50:22,750
Not like this.

1348
01:50:22,830 --> 01:50:24,250
You should see the nurse.

1349
01:50:24,370 --> 01:50:25,830
I think it's a warning.

1350
01:50:25,920 --> 01:50:28,080
It means danger's coming.

1351
01:50:35,260 --> 01:50:37,970
-Of course!   -What is it?

1352
01:50:37,970 --> 01:50:38,580
Isn't it odd

1353
01:50:38,580 --> 01:50:41,890
that what Hagrid wants more than anything is a dragon...

1354
01:50:41,890 --> 01:50:44,640
...and a stranger just happens to have one?

1355
01:50:44,640 --> 01:50:48,150
How many people wander around with dragon eggs?

1356
01:50:48,150 --> 01:50:50,990
Why didn't I see it before?

1357
01:50:56,030 --> 01:50:58,320
Hagrid. Who gave you the dragon egg?

1358
01:50:58,320 --> 01:50:59,660
What did he look like?

1359
01:50:59,780 --> 01:51:01,780
I don't know. I never saw his face.

1360
01:51:01,870 --> 01:51:02,620
He kept his hood up.

1361
01:51:02,740 --> 01:51:05,870
You and this stranger must have talked.

1362
01:51:05,960 --> 01:51:09,630
He wanted to know what sort of creatures I looked after.

1363
01:51:09,750 --> 01:51:11,880
I told him,"I feed fter Fluffy,

1364
01:51:12,000 --> 01:51:13,880
a dragon's gonna be no problem."

1365
01:51:13,960 --> 01:51:16,170
Was he interested in Fluffy?

1366
01:51:16,340 --> 01:51:18,630
Of course he was interested in Fluffy.

1367
01:51:18,720 --> 01:51:20,930
How often do you come across a three-headed dog?

1368
01:51:20,930 --> 01:51:23,010
Even the rare creatures trade

1369
01:51:23,140 --> 01:51:24,680
But I told him,

1370
01:51:24,770 --> 01:51:27,060
The trick with any beast

1371
01:51:27,180 --> 01:51:28,810
is to know how to calm him.

1372
01:51:28,940 --> 01:51:30,770
Take Fluffy, for example.

1373
01:51:30,770 --> 01:51:31,860
Play him music

1374
01:51:31,980 --> 01:51:33,520
and he falls straight to sleep.

1375
01:51:36,070 --> 01:51:38,860
I shouldn't have told you that.

1376
01:51:38,860 --> 01:51:41,700
Where are you going? Where are you going?

1377
01:51:48,000 --> 01:51:49,870
We have to see Dumbledore.

1378
01:51:49,870 --> 01:51:51,290
Immediately!

1379
01:51:51,380 --> 01:51:54,090
I'm afraid he's not here.

1380
01:51:54,250 --> 01:51:58,720
He received an urgent owl from the Ministry of Magic and left.

1381
01:51:58,840 --> 01:52:00,180
He's gone?

1382
01:52:00,180 --> 01:52:01,890
But this is important!

1383
01:52:01,970 --> 01:52:05,810
This is about the Sorcerer's Stone!

1384
01:52:05,810 --> 01:52:10,100
-How do you know...?   -Someone's going to try and steal it.

1385
01:52:10,190 --> 01:52:12,310
I don't know how you know,

1386
01:52:12,310 --> 01:52:15,020
but I assure you it is well protected.

1387
01:52:15,570 --> 01:52:18,150
Now would you go back to your dormitories?

1388
01:52:18,150 --> 01:52:19,360
Quietly.

1389
01:52:28,290 --> 01:52:30,250
That was no stranger Hagrid met.

1390
01:52:30,370 --> 01:52:31,290
It was Snape.

1391
01:52:31,370 --> 01:52:33,830
Which means he knows how to get past Fluffy.

1392
01:52:33,920 --> 01:52:35,500
And with Dumbledore gone...

1393
01:52:35,500 --> 01:52:37,170
Good afternoon.

1394
01:52:40,010 --> 01:52:43,340
What would three young Gryffindors...

1395
01:52:43,470 --> 01:52:49,600
...be doing inside on a day like this?

1396
01:52:49,600 --> 01:52:53,810
We were just...

1397
01:52:53,810 --> 01:52:55,860
You ought to be careful.

1398
01:52:56,440 --> 01:52:59,010
People will think you're...

1399
01:53:02,740 --> 01:53:05,950
...up to something.

1400
01:53:15,630 --> 01:53:18,130
Now what do we do?

1401
01:53:18,130 --> 01:53:19,840
We go down the trap door.

1402
01:53:20,090 --> 01:53:21,340
Tonight.

1403
01:53:35,520 --> 01:53:37,190
Trevor.

1404
01:53:37,310 --> 01:53:38,360
Trevor,

1405
01:53:38,480 --> 01:53:39,940
go! You shouldn't be here!

1406
01:53:41,110 --> 01:53:42,740
Neither should you.

1407
01:53:44,200 --> 01:53:46,410
You're sneaking out again, aren't you?

1408
01:53:46,530 --> 01:53:48,450
Neville, listen. We were...

1409
01:53:48,450 --> 01:53:50,750
No, I won't let you!

1410
01:53:50,870 --> 01:53:53,080
You'll get Gryffindor into trouble again.

1411
01:53:53,210 --> 01:53:55,540
I'll fight you.

1412
01:53:55,670 --> 01:53:57,960
Neville, I'm really sorry about this.

1413
01:53:58,090 --> 01:54:00,050
Petrificus Totalus.

1414
01:54:07,890 --> 01:54:10,310
You're a little scary sometimes,

1415
01:54:10,390 --> 01:54:11,770
you know that?

1416
01:54:11,890 --> 01:54:16,060
Brilliant, but scary.

1417
01:54:16,350 --> 01:54:17,520
Let's go.

1418
01:54:18,520 --> 01:54:22,230
-Sorry.   -It's for your own good, you know.

1419
01:54:28,070 --> 01:54:30,160
You stood on my foot!

1420
01:54:30,160 --> 01:54:31,410
Sorry.

1421
01:54:35,960 --> 01:54:37,710
Alohomora.

1422
01:54:50,140 --> 01:54:52,560
Wait a minute. He's...

1423
01:54:53,810 --> 01:54:56,100
...snoring.

1424
01:54:58,560 --> 01:55:00,440
Snape's already been here.

1425
01:55:01,400 --> 01:55:03,440
He's put a spell on the harp.

1426
01:55:04,650 --> 01:55:09,140
It's got horrible breath.

1427
01:55:11,280 --> 01:55:12,540
We have to move its paw.

1428
01:55:12,660 --> 01:55:13,540
What?

1429
01:55:13,620 --> 01:55:14,700
Come on!

1430
01:55:18,870 --> 01:55:21,550
Okay. Push.

1431
01:55:44,230 --> 01:55:45,530
I'll go first.

1432
01:55:45,650 --> 01:55:47,780
Don't follow until I give you a sign.

1433
01:55:48,110 --> 01:55:49,700
If something bad happens,

1434
01:55:49,820 --> 01:55:52,200
get yourselves out.

1435
01:55:53,830 --> 01:55:57,910
Does it seem a bit quiet to you?

1436
01:55:58,120 --> 01:55:59,960
The harp.

1437
01:56:00,830 --> 01:56:02,460
It's stopped playing.

1438
01:56:13,550 --> 01:56:15,640
Jump!

1439
01:56:28,530 --> 01:56:32,730
Lucky this plant thing's here, really.

1440
01:56:46,880 --> 01:56:48,460
Stop moving, both of you.

1441
01:56:48,590 --> 01:56:49,920
This is Devil's Snare.

1442
01:56:50,050 --> 01:56:51,340
You have to relax.

1443
01:56:51,470 --> 01:56:53,840
If you don't, it will only kill you faster.

1444
01:56:53,930 --> 01:56:55,300
Ikill us faster?

1445
01:56:55,390 --> 01:56:57,850
Oh, now I can relax!

1446
01:57:01,190 --> 01:57:02,810
Hermione!

1447
01:57:03,020 --> 01:57:04,400
Now what are we gonna do?

1448
01:57:04,520 --> 01:57:06,270
Just relax!

1449
01:57:07,020 --> 01:57:08,860
Hermione, where are you?

1450
01:57:08,860 --> 01:57:10,440
Do what I say!

1451
01:57:10,570 --> 01:57:11,950
Trust me.

1452
01:57:15,240 --> 01:57:16,410
Harry!

1453
01:57:16,950 --> 01:57:18,240
Harry!

1454
01:57:18,700 --> 01:57:19,500
Are you okay?

1455
01:57:19,620 --> 01:57:20,870
Yeah, I'm fine.

1456
01:57:22,160 --> 01:57:23,870
He's not relaxing, is he?

1457
01:57:23,870 --> 01:57:25,330
Apparently not.

1458
01:57:25,420 --> 01:57:27,460
-We've gotta do something.   -What?

1459
01:57:27,460 --> 01:57:31,630
I remember reading something in Herbology.

1460
01:57:32,130 --> 01:57:33,590
Devil's Snare, Devil's Snare.

1461
01:57:33,680 --> 01:57:35,850
It's deadly fun...

1462
01:57:35,970 --> 01:57:37,560
...but will sulk in the sun!

1463
01:57:37,560 --> 01:57:40,270
That's it! It hates sunlight.

1464
01:57:40,600 --> 01:57:43,230
Lumus Solem.

1465
01:57:50,820 --> 01:57:51,740
Ron, you okay?

1466
01:57:51,860 --> 01:57:53,070
Yeah.

1467
01:57:55,990 --> 01:57:59,040
Lucky we didn't panic.

1468
01:57:59,160 --> 01:58:03,310
Lucky Hermione pays attention in Herbology.

1469
01:58:04,460 --> 01:58:05,920
What is that?

1470
01:58:06,000 --> 01:58:08,380
I don't know.

1471
01:58:08,380 --> 01:58:09,550
Sounds like wings.

1472
01:58:23,100 --> 01:58:24,140
Curious.

1473
01:58:24,270 --> 01:58:26,480
I've never seen birds like these.

1474
01:58:26,690 --> 01:58:30,360
They're not birds. They're keys.

1475
01:58:30,480 --> 01:58:34,480
And I'll bet one of them fits that door.

1476
01:58:37,370 --> 01:58:39,620
What's this all about?

1477
01:58:39,620 --> 01:58:41,330
I don't know.

1478
01:58:48,130 --> 01:58:49,540
Strange.

1479
01:58:50,420 --> 01:58:52,210
Alohomora!

1480
01:58:55,550 --> 01:58:58,180
Well, it was worth a try.

1481
01:58:58,180 --> 01:58:59,600
What will we do?

1482
01:58:59,680 --> 01:59:01,510
There must be a thousand keys.

1483
01:59:01,600 --> 01:59:03,850
We want a big, old-fashioned one.

1484
01:59:03,930 --> 01:59:05,350
Probably rusty.

1485
01:59:05,430 --> 01:59:07,230
I see it!

1486
01:59:07,230 --> 01:59:09,020
The one with the broken wing.

1487
01:59:12,570 --> 01:59:15,560
What's wrong?

1488
01:59:16,070 --> 01:59:17,570
It's too simple.

1489
01:59:17,700 --> 01:59:19,370
Go on!

1490
01:59:19,450 --> 01:59:21,080
If Snape could catch it on that old broomstick,

1491
01:59:21,200 --> 01:59:22,540
you can.

1492
01:59:22,620 --> 01:59:25,330
You're the youngest Seeker in a century.

1493
01:59:43,010 --> 01:59:45,060
This complicates things a bit.

1494
02:00:07,290 --> 02:00:08,660
Catch the key!

1495
02:00:13,540 --> 02:00:16,020
Hurry up!

1496
02:00:47,950 --> 02:00:51,000
I don't like this.

1497
02:00:51,000 --> 02:00:52,880
I don't like this at all.

1498
02:00:52,960 --> 02:00:54,380
Where are we?

1499
02:00:54,710 --> 02:00:56,300
A graveyard?

1500
02:00:56,420 --> 02:00:59,560
This is no graveyard.

1501
02:01:06,510 --> 02:01:10,010
It's a chessboard.

1502
02:01:21,400 --> 02:01:23,890
There's the door.

1503
02:01:35,630 --> 02:01:37,170
Now what do we do?

1504
02:01:37,250 --> 02:01:38,750
It's obvious, isn't it?

1505
02:01:38,750 --> 02:01:40,800
We've got to play our way across the room.

1506
02:01:42,050 --> 02:01:43,050
All right.

1507
02:01:43,180 --> 02:01:46,050
Harry, you take the empty bishop's square.

1508
02:01:46,140 --> 02:01:50,520
Hermione, you'll be the queen-side castle.

1509
02:01:50,520 --> 02:01:52,440
As for me,

1510
02:01:52,440 --> 02:01:54,100
I'll be a knight.

1511
02:02:01,650 --> 02:02:04,030
What happens now?

1512
02:02:04,280 --> 02:02:07,280
Well, white moves first.

1513
02:02:07,490 --> 02:02:09,870
And then...

1514
02:02:11,040 --> 02:02:12,910
...we play.

1515
02:02:22,880 --> 02:02:24,550
Ron,

1516
02:02:24,550 --> 02:02:27,640
you don't suppose this is going to be like...

1517
02:02:27,720 --> 02:02:32,140
...real wizard's chess, do you?

1518
02:02:32,140 --> 02:02:35,660
You there, D-5.

1519
02:02:49,780 --> 02:02:51,540
Yes, Hermione.

1520
02:02:51,540 --> 02:02:54,210
I think this is gonna be

1521
02:02:54,210 --> 02:02:56,500
exactly like wizard's chess.

1522
02:03:02,340 --> 02:03:05,580
Castle to E-4!

1523
02:03:08,590 --> 02:03:11,220
Pawn to C-3!

1524
02:03:55,770 --> 02:03:57,640
Wait a minute.

1525
02:03:57,770 --> 02:03:59,850
You understand right, Harry.

1526
02:03:59,980 --> 02:04:02,400
Once I make my move,

1527
02:04:02,480 --> 02:04:05,070
the queen will take me.

1528
02:04:05,190 --> 02:04:07,570
Then you're free to check the king.

1529
02:04:07,570 --> 02:04:09,530
No. Ron, no!

1530
02:04:09,530 --> 02:04:10,950
What is it?

1531
02:04:11,070 --> 02:04:12,740
He's going to sacrifice himself.

1532
02:04:12,740 --> 02:04:15,700
No, there must be another way!

1533
02:04:15,790 --> 02:04:19,870
Do you wanna stop Snape from getting that Stone or not?

1534
02:04:19,870 --> 02:04:22,380
Harry, it's you that has to go on.

1535
02:04:22,380 --> 02:04:23,790
I know it.

1536
02:04:23,920 --> 02:04:27,300
Not me. Not Hermione. You.

1537
02:04:37,140 --> 02:04:39,890
Knight to H-3.

1538
02:05:00,870 --> 02:05:03,370
Check.

1539
02:05:31,990 --> 02:05:34,030
Ron!

1540
02:05:34,030 --> 02:05:36,030
No, don't move!

1541
02:05:36,030 --> 02:05:38,870
Don't forget, we're still playing.

1542
02:05:54,970 --> 02:05:56,510
Checkmate.

1543
02:06:16,160 --> 02:06:17,410
Take care of Ron.

1544
02:06:17,530 --> 02:06:18,740
Then go to the owlery.

1545
02:06:18,870 --> 02:06:20,750
Send a message to Dumbledore.

1546
02:06:20,910 --> 02:06:22,750
Ron's right.

1547
02:06:22,910 --> 02:06:24,170
I have to go on.

1548
02:06:25,210 --> 02:06:27,590
You'll be okay, Harry.

1549
02:06:27,590 --> 02:06:29,210
You're a great wizard.

1550
02:06:29,340 --> 02:06:30,840
You really are.

1551
02:06:31,550 --> 02:06:33,050
Not as good as you.

1552
02:06:34,800 --> 02:06:37,760
Me? Books and cleverness.

1553
02:06:37,760 --> 02:06:40,510
There are more important things.

1554
02:06:40,770 --> 02:06:44,060
Friendship and bravery.

1555
02:06:44,060 --> 02:06:46,520
And, Harry, just be careful.

1556
02:07:24,390 --> 02:07:26,710
You?

1557
02:07:27,350 --> 02:07:29,440
No, it can't be.

1558
02:07:29,520 --> 02:07:30,980
Snape, he was the...

1559
02:07:31,110 --> 02:07:34,280
Yes, he does seem the type, doesn't he?

1560
02:07:34,360 --> 02:07:36,490
Next to him,

1561
02:07:36,570 --> 02:07:41,200
who would suspect poor, stuttering Professor Quirrell?

1562
02:07:41,200 --> 02:07:45,540
But that day, during the Quidditch match,

1563
02:07:45,540 --> 02:07:46,870
Snape tried to kill me.

1564
02:07:46,960 --> 02:07:48,670
No, dear boy.

1565
02:07:48,670 --> 02:07:50,580
I tried to kill you!

1566
02:07:50,710 --> 02:07:51,790
And trust me.

1567
02:07:51,880 --> 02:07:54,260
If Snape's cloak hadn't caught fire

1568
02:07:54,340 --> 02:07:55,460
and broken my eye contact...

1569
02:07:55,550 --> 02:07:57,380
...I would have succeeded.

1570
02:07:57,510 --> 02:08:00,760
Even with Snape muttering his countercurse.

1571
02:08:00,890 --> 02:08:03,060
Snape was trying to save me?

1572
02:08:03,140 --> 02:08:05,520
I knew you were a danger to me,

1573
02:08:05,600 --> 02:08:08,100
especially after Halloween.

1574
02:08:08,390 --> 02:08:10,810
Then you let the troll in!

1575
02:08:10,810 --> 02:08:12,900
Very good, Potter, yes.

1576
02:08:13,230 --> 02:08:16,610
Snape, unfortunately, wasn't fooled.

1577
02:08:16,690 --> 02:08:18,650
While everyone ran about,

1578
02:08:18,740 --> 02:08:21,120
he went to the third floor to head me off.

1579
02:08:22,490 --> 02:08:26,580
He, of course, never trusted me again.

1580
02:08:27,000 --> 02:08:29,580
He rarely left me alone.

1581
02:08:29,580 --> 02:08:31,830
But he doesn't understand.

1582
02:08:32,460 --> 02:08:36,710
I'm never alone. Never.

1583
02:08:36,710 --> 02:08:38,090
Now,

1584
02:08:38,090 --> 02:08:40,590
what does this mirror do?

1585
02:08:42,390 --> 02:08:45,060
I see what I desire.

1586
02:08:45,100 --> 02:08:48,230
I see myself holding the Stone.

1587
02:08:48,230 --> 02:08:49,890
But how do I get it?

1588
02:08:50,020 --> 02:08:52,100
Use the boy.

1589
02:08:52,650 --> 02:08:54,980
Come here, Potter!

1590
02:08:54,980 --> 02:08:56,400
Now!

1591
02:09:08,660 --> 02:09:10,290
Tell me,

1592
02:09:10,290 --> 02:09:12,120
what do you see?

1593
02:09:37,780 --> 02:09:39,860
What is it? What do you see?

1594
02:09:39,860 --> 02:09:43,410
I'm shaking hands with Dumbledore.

1595
02:09:43,410 --> 02:09:45,830
I've won the house cup.

1596
02:09:45,950 --> 02:09:47,830
He lies.

1597
02:09:47,950 --> 02:09:49,660
Tell the truth!

1598
02:09:49,790 --> 02:09:51,750
What do you see?

1599
02:09:51,870 --> 02:09:54,330
Let me speak to him.

1600
02:09:54,420 --> 02:09:56,210
Master, you are not strong enough.

1601
02:09:56,340 --> 02:10:01,000
I have strength enough for this.

1602
02:10:18,610 --> 02:10:21,740
Harry Potter...

1603
02:10:21,740 --> 02:10:24,240
...we meet again.

1604
02:10:24,360 --> 02:10:25,820
Voldemort.

1605
02:10:25,950 --> 02:10:27,450
Yes.

1606
02:10:27,580 --> 02:10:30,160
You see what I've become?

1607
02:10:30,240 --> 02:10:34,580
See what I must do to survive?

1608
02:10:34,670 --> 02:10:36,420
Live off another.

1609
02:10:36,500 --> 02:10:38,670
A mere parasite.

1610
02:10:38,790 --> 02:10:42,470
Unicorn blood can sustain me...

1611
02:10:42,590 --> 02:10:45,930
...but it cannot give me a body of my own.

1612
02:10:46,090 --> 02:10:50,010
But there is something that can.

1613
02:10:50,010 --> 02:10:53,520
Something that, conveniently enough,

1614
02:10:53,640 --> 02:10:55,190
lies in your pocket.

1615
02:10:55,690 --> 02:10:58,020
Stop him!

1616
02:11:02,530 --> 02:11:04,650
Don't be a fool.

1617
02:11:05,450 --> 02:11:12,950
Why suffer an horrific death when you can join me and live?

1618
02:11:13,080 --> 02:11:14,370
Never!

1619
02:11:15,870 --> 02:11:18,210
Bravery.

1620
02:11:18,210 --> 02:11:21,300
Your parents had it too.

1621
02:11:21,500 --> 02:11:23,340
Tell me,

1622
02:11:23,340 --> 02:11:24,760
Harry...

1623
02:11:25,090 --> 02:11:29,100
...would you like to see your mother and father again?

1624
02:11:29,100 --> 02:11:31,560
Together...

1625
02:11:31,560 --> 02:11:34,430
...we can bring them back.

1626
02:11:34,560 --> 02:11:39,310
All I ask is for something in return.

1627
02:11:46,070 --> 02:11:49,660
That's it, Harry.

1628
02:11:50,070 --> 02:11:53,910
There is no good and evil.

1629
02:11:54,120 --> 02:11:57,370
There is only power...

1630
02:11:57,500 --> 02:12:01,790
...and those too weak to seek it.

1631
02:12:02,170 --> 02:12:03,750
Together,

1632
02:12:03,800 --> 02:12:07,510
we'll do extraordinary things.

1633
02:12:07,630 --> 02:12:11,100
Just give me the Stone!

1634
02:12:12,470 --> 02:12:13,810
You liar!

1635
02:12:13,890 --> 02:12:15,470
Kill him!

1636
02:12:39,460 --> 02:12:41,210
What is this magic?

1637
02:12:41,210 --> 02:12:44,130
Fool, get the Stone!

1638
02:14:30,030 --> 02:14:31,900
Good afternoon, Harry.

1639
02:14:34,700 --> 02:14:37,660
Tokens from your admirers?

1640
02:14:37,780 --> 02:14:39,240
Admirers?

1641
02:14:39,370 --> 02:14:43,420
What happened in the dungeons between you and Professor Quirrell

1642
02:14:43,420 --> 02:14:45,420
is a uncompleted secret.

1643
02:14:45,540 --> 02:14:50,890
So, naturally, the whole school knows.

1644
02:14:52,590 --> 02:14:55,380
I see that your friend Ronald has saved you the trouble...

1645
02:14:55,380 --> 02:14:59,640
...of opening your Chocolate Frogs.

1646
02:14:59,640 --> 02:15:01,720
Ron was here? Is he all right?

1647
02:15:01,720 --> 02:15:02,730
What about Hermione?

1648
02:15:02,850 --> 02:15:04,640
Fine.

1649
02:15:04,850 --> 02:15:07,270
They're both just fine.

1650
02:15:07,980 --> 02:15:09,570
What happened to the Stone?

1651
02:15:09,570 --> 02:15:11,360
Relax, dear boy.

1652
02:15:11,480 --> 02:15:13,900
The Stone has been destroyed.

1653
02:15:14,740 --> 02:15:17,620
My friend Nicholas and I have had a little chat...

1654
02:15:17,740 --> 02:15:23,080
...and agreed it was best all around.

1655
02:15:23,080 --> 02:15:27,430
But then, Flamel, he'll die, won't he?

1656
02:15:29,000 --> 02:15:32,250
He has enough Elixir

1657
02:15:32,250 --> 02:15:34,260
to set his affairs in order.

1658
02:15:34,670 --> 02:15:36,590
But yes,

1659
02:15:36,590 --> 02:15:38,300
he will die.

1660
02:15:38,430 --> 02:15:40,600
How is it I got the Stone, sir?

1661
02:15:40,680 --> 02:15:42,470
One minute I was staring in the mirror

1662
02:15:42,470 --> 02:15:43,640
and...

1663
02:15:43,770 --> 02:15:47,770
You see, only a person...

1664
02:15:47,900 --> 02:15:52,150
...who wanted to find the Stone, find it...

1665
02:15:52,230 --> 02:15:53,900
...but not use it,

1666
02:15:53,980 --> 02:15:56,530
would be able to get it.

1667
02:15:57,610 --> 02:16:01,580
That is one of my more brilliant ideas.

1668
02:16:01,700 --> 02:16:03,540
And between you and me,

1669
02:16:03,620 --> 02:16:06,290
that is saying something.

1670
02:16:07,790 --> 02:16:10,920
Does that mean, with the Stone gone,

1671
02:16:11,040 --> 02:16:13,130
that Voldemort can never come back?

1672
02:16:13,250 --> 02:16:16,080
I'm afraid...

1673
02:16:16,920 --> 02:16:21,540
...there are ways in which he can return.

1674
02:16:21,760 --> 02:16:22,930
Harry,

1675
02:16:22,930 --> 02:16:25,020
do you know why...

1676
02:16:25,020 --> 02:16:28,730
...Professor Quirrell couldn't bear to have you touch him?

1677
02:16:28,730 --> 02:16:31,190
It was because of your mother.

1678
02:16:31,190 --> 02:16:33,860
She sacrificed herself for you.

1679
02:16:33,980 --> 02:16:37,280
And that kind of act leaves a mark.

1680
02:16:37,400 --> 02:16:41,280
No, this kind of mark cannot be seen.

1681
02:16:41,410 --> 02:16:44,410
It lives in your very skin.

1682
02:16:44,540 --> 02:16:46,580
What is it?

1683
02:16:47,160 --> 02:16:50,920
Love, Harry. Love.

1684
02:16:58,800 --> 02:17:03,260
Bertie Bott's Every Flavor Beans.

1685
02:17:03,260 --> 02:17:05,810
I was most unfortunate in my youth

1686
02:17:05,810 --> 02:17:07,980
to come across a vomit-flavored one.

1687
02:17:08,230 --> 02:17:11,560
And since then, I've lost my liking for them.

1688
02:17:11,650 --> 02:17:15,480
But I think I could be safe...

1689
02:17:15,480 --> 02:17:17,070
...with a nice toffee.

1690
02:17:21,610 --> 02:17:23,770
Alas!

1691
02:17:23,870 --> 02:17:26,540
Earwax.

1692
02:17:41,260 --> 02:17:42,760
All right there, Ron?

1693
02:17:42,760 --> 02:17:44,970
All right. You?

1694
02:17:45,510 --> 02:17:47,390
All right.

1695
02:17:47,390 --> 02:17:48,470
Hermione?

1696
02:17:48,560 --> 02:17:51,340
Never better.

1697
02:18:06,580 --> 02:18:09,620
Another year gone.

1698
02:18:09,910 --> 02:18:11,910
And now, as I understand it,

1699
02:18:12,000 --> 02:18:14,290
the house cup needs awarding.

1700
02:18:14,420 --> 02:18:17,590
And the points stand thus:

1701
02:18:17,590 --> 02:18:19,050
In fourth place,

1702
02:18:19,170 --> 02:18:22,550
Gryffindor with 312 points.

1703
02:18:25,220 --> 02:18:27,050
Third place,

1704
02:18:27,140 --> 02:18:31,520
Hufflepuff with 352 points.

1705
02:18:35,980 --> 02:18:38,190
In second place...

1706
02:18:38,190 --> 02:18:43,070
...Ravenclaw with 426 points.

1707
02:18:48,830 --> 02:18:50,660
And in first place...

1708
02:18:50,790 --> 02:18:53,500
...with 472 points,

1709
02:18:53,620 --> 02:18:55,460
Slytherin house.

1710
02:19:01,670 --> 02:19:04,380
Nice one, mate.

1711
02:19:07,680 --> 02:19:09,890
Yes, well done, Slytherin. Well done.

1712
02:19:09,890 --> 02:19:10,810
Slytherin. Well done.

1713
02:19:10,930 --> 02:19:12,100
However,

1714
02:19:12,180 --> 02:19:16,310
recent events must be taken into account.

1715
02:19:16,440 --> 02:19:22,060
And I have a few last-minute points to award.

1716
02:19:22,190 --> 02:19:25,360
To Miss Hermione Granger,

1717
02:19:25,360 --> 02:19:31,200
for the cool use of intellect while others were in grave peril...

1718
02:19:31,330 --> 02:19:34,140
...50 points.

1719
02:19:34,580 --> 02:19:36,380
Good job.

1720
02:19:43,590 --> 02:19:47,590
Second, to Mr. Ronald Weasley,

1721
02:19:47,720 --> 02:19:50,050
for the best-played game of chess...

1722
02:19:50,180 --> 02:19:54,520
...that Hogwarts has seen these many years,

1723
02:19:54,600 --> 02:19:56,190
50 points.

1724
02:20:00,110 --> 02:20:02,530
And third...

1725
02:20:02,650 --> 02:20:05,610
...to Mr. Harry Potter...

1726
02:20:05,700 --> 02:20:10,450
...for pure nerve and outstanding courage...

1727
02:20:10,530 --> 02:20:14,080
...I award Gryffindor house

1728
02:20:14,080 --> 02:20:15,870
60 points.

1729
02:20:23,800 --> 02:20:25,800
We're tied with Slytherin!

1730
02:20:25,920 --> 02:20:27,590
Finally,

1731
02:20:27,630 --> 02:20:32,050
it takes a great deal of bravery to stand up to your enemies...

1732
02:20:32,180 --> 02:20:35,640
...but a great deal more to stand up to your friends.

1733
02:20:36,100 --> 02:20:36,680
I award 10 points...

1734
02:20:36,680 --> 02:20:41,980
...to Neville Longbottom.

1735
02:20:53,910 --> 02:20:58,580
Assuming that my calculations are correct I believe...

1736
02:20:58,710 --> 02:21:04,560
...that a change of decoration is in order.

1737
02:21:09,050 --> 02:21:12,970
Gryffindor wins the house cup.

1738
02:21:48,630 --> 02:21:52,010
Come on, now. Hurry up, you'll be late.

1739
02:21:52,010 --> 02:21:54,510
Train's leaving. Go on. Go on.

1740
02:21:54,510 --> 02:21:57,220
Come on, hurry up.

1741
02:22:03,000 --> 02:22:03,540
Come on, Harry.

1742
02:22:03,540 --> 02:22:05,500
One minute.

1743
02:22:12,720 --> 02:22:15,590
Thought you were leaving without saying goodbye, did you?

1744
02:22:20,200 --> 02:22:21,820
This is for you.

1745
02:22:38,630 --> 02:22:39,970
Thanks, Hagrid.

1746
02:22:46,560 --> 02:22:49,560
Go on. On with you. On with you now.

1747
02:22:49,560 --> 02:22:51,230
Oh, listen, Harry.

1748
02:22:51,440 --> 02:22:52,770
If that dolt of a cousin of yours,

1749
02:22:52,850 --> 02:22:55,190
Dudley, gives you any grief...

1750
02:22:56,110 --> 02:22:58,900
...you could always threaten him...

1751
02:22:59,030 --> 02:23:01,990
...with a nice pair of ears to go with his tail.

1752
02:23:02,110 --> 02:23:04,870
But we're not allowed to do magic away from Hogwarts.

1753
02:23:04,870 --> 02:23:07,370
You know that.

1754
02:23:07,490 --> 02:23:09,120
I do.

1755
02:23:09,120 --> 02:23:17,550
But your cousin don't, do he?

1756
02:23:17,550 --> 02:23:20,720
Feels strange to be going home, doesn't it?

1757
02:23:20,880 --> 02:23:22,630
I'm not going home.

1758
02:23:23,090 --> 02:23:25,540
Not really.

